hen_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"The reserve holds Mexico''s highest jaguar density and 365+ bird species","si":"expedition","blurb":"The reserve holds Mexico''s highest jaguar density and 365+ bird species","when":"November–April","commission":"licensed wildlife-guide add-on, DMC-bundled"},{"name":"Bat Cave (Volcán de los Murciélagos) dusk exodus","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"essential","commission_path":"dusk-timed guided add-on / DMC evening leg","source":"https://www.beyondtheordinary.co.uk/features/calakmul-bat-cave/","timing":"November–April","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"One of only two \"bat volcano\" spectacles on Earth","si":"expedition","blurb":"One of only two \"bat volcano\" spectacles on Earth","when":"November–April","commission":"dusk-timed guided add-on / DMC evening leg"},{"name":"Birding — 350+ species","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"comfort","commission_path":"specialist birding-guide day, DMC-bundled","source":"http://world-heritage-datasheets.unep-wcmc.org/datasheet/output/site/ancient-maya-city-and-protected-tropical-forests-of-calakmul-campeche/","timing":"November–April","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"From ocellated turkey to keel-billed toucan to raptors over the canopy; the reserve is a top Yucatán-Peninsula birding target","si":"expedition","blurb":"From ocellated turkey to keel-billed toucan to raptors over the canopy; the reserve is a top Yucatán-Peninsula birding target","when":"November–April","commission":"specialist birding-guide day, DMC-bundled"},{"name":"Río Bec route — Becán, Chicanná, Xpujil, Balamkú (16.8 m stucco frieze)","si_tag":"culture","tier":"essential","commission_path":"heritage day-loop add-on, DMC-bundled","source":"https://lostruinsoftheamericas.com/balamku/","timing":"November–April","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"A corridor of Río Bec-style ruins: theatrical false towers, rounded corners, and monster-mouth doorways, all within short drives of Xpujil","si":"culture","blurb":"A corridor of Río Bec-style ruins: theatrical false towers, rounded corners, and monster-mouth doorways, all within short drives of Xpujil","when":"November–April","commission":"heritage day-loop add-on, DMC-bundled"},{"name":"Calakmul as Snake Kingdom (Kaan) capital — Tikal rivalry narrative","si_tag":"culture","tier":"comfort","commission_path":"archaeologist-led interpretive guiding, DMC premium","source":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Calakmul","timing":"November–April","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"The narrative jewel: seat of the Kaan dynasty","si":"culture","blurb":"The narrative jewel: seat of the Kaan dynasty","when":"November–April","commission":"archaeologist-led interpretive guiding, DMC premium"},{"name":"Zoh-Laguna village nature base","si_tag":"wildlife","tier":"essential","commission_path":"small-lodge stay + local guide","source":"https://riobecdreams.com/","timing":"November–April","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"wildlife","when":"November–April","commission":"small-lodge stay + local guide"},{"name":"Tren Maya arrival (Xpujil station)","si_tag":"wildlife","commission_path":"rail affiliate + DMC meet-and-transfer","source":"https://www.mexicotravelandleisure.com/blog/maya-train-route-and-guide/","timing":"November–April","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"The rail arrival is itself a jewel now: glide inland from Cancún/Palenque to Xpujil, then transfer to the jungle","si":"wildlife","blurb":"The rail arrival is itself a jewel now: glide inland from Cancún/Palenque to Xpujil, then transfer to the jungle","when":"November–April","commission":"rail affiliate + DMC meet-and-transfer"}],"faq":[{"q":"Is Calakmul safe to visit?","a":"Yes — freely bookable, with the right logistics. Campeche is one of only two Mexican states at US State Dept Level 1 \"Exercise Normal Precautions,\" and there are no US-government travel restrictions in the state. The real risks here are wilderness and logistics, not the security profile that drives higher Mexican advisories.","source":"travel.state.gov, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"What''s the real risk to plan for at Calakmul?","a":"The drive itself. The reserve is 60–110 km of narrow, unlit jungle road past the last fuel and signal at Xpujil, with a ~30 km/h wildlife limit and no in-reserve hospital — serious trauma means a 2–4 hr evacuation to Campeche City or Chetumal. Carry evacuation-grade insurance, fuel up in Xpujil, and note that rural Campeche is a CDC malaria-prophylaxis (P. vivax) state with dengue present, so bite prevention matters.","source":"casakaan.com / wwwnc.cdc.gov, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"What is the Structure II pyramid climb like?","a":"A 45 m (148 ft) ascent on steep, uneven ancient stone, best done at first light before the tropical heat. There are no railings and the stone is slick after rain, so climb early, go with a guide for pacing, and descend facing the steps. The payoff is a canopy that rolls out like a green sea, with howler monkeys roaring in the trees below.","source":"en.wikipedia.org, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"expedition"},{"q":"Will I actually see jaguars and wildlife?","a":"You''ll see plenty, though jaguars are rare. The reserve holds Mexico''s highest jaguar density but sightings are uncommon; on a pre-dawn drive you reliably get howler and spider monkeys, toucans and many of the 365+ bird species as the canopy wakes. Stay on marked routes with a licensed guide — no approach, no touch, no feeding, and watch for fer-de-lance in the leaf litter.","source":"unep-wcmc.org, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"wildlife"},{"q":"What is the Calakmul Bat Cave?","a":"Volcán de los Murciélagos, one of only two \"bat volcano\" spectacles on Earth: an estimated 2–5 million bats erupt in a swirling vortex about an hour before dusk, off Highway 186 near km 107. Time it with a guide so the drive back out is managed in the dark, wear repellent at peak biting hour, and pack a headlamp.","source":"beyondtheordinary.co.uk, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"expedition"},{"q":"Why does Calakmul matter historically?","a":"It was the capital of the Snake Kingdom (the Kaan dynasty), the Maya superpower whose two-century rivalry with Tikal defined the Classic period until Calakmul''s defeat in 695 CE. It is a UNESCO mixed World Heritage site — culture (2002) and nature (2014) on one deed — and the nearby Río Bec route adds Becán, Chicanná, Xpujil and Balamkú''s 16.8 m stucco frieze.","source":"whc.unesco.org, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"culture"},{"q":"How do I get to Calakmul, and does the Tren Maya reach it?","a":"The Tren Maya''s Xpujil station has run since December 2024, connecting the jungle base town to Palenque, Campeche, Bacalar and Cancún — but the final 60–110 km into the reserve is still a car. Critically, book the Xpujil station, not the isolated \"Calakmul\"-named halt, which leaves travelers stranded without services.","source":"mexicotravelandleisure.com / casakaan.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"access"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"Calakmul, Mexico: The Lost Maya City in the Jungle — Ruins, Jaguars & the Bat Cave | TravelWell","search_language":"es-MX","local_keywords":["ruinas de Calakmul","reserva de la biosfera Calakmul","Río Bec Xpujil","cómo llegar a Calakmul","Estructura II Calakmul pirámide","Volcán de los Murciélagos Calakmul","Tren Maya estación Xpujil"],"hreflang":["en","es-MX"],"jsonld_type":"TouristDestination","author_byline":"By David McCallister — commercial pilot, 56 countries","freshness":"2026-07-07","primary_keyword":"Calakmul"},"booking":null,"si_checklist_25":null,"sis_present":[{"si":"culture","status":"live"},{"si":"wildlife","status":"live"},{"si":"expedition","status":"live"}],"ultra":[{"property":"Hotel Puerta Calakmul","type":"cabaña lodge at reserve gate","mor":"direct/DMC","tier":"mid (ceiling)","earning":"small-property commission; value = proximity"},{"property":"Río Bec Dreams","type":"7-Jungalow eco-lodge near Becán/Chicanná","mor":"direct/DMC","tier":"comfort","earning":"direct commission; strong for Río Bec route"},{"property":"Zoh-Laguna / Xpujil cabañas","type":"village cabañas / small hotels","mor":"bedbank/direct","tier":"essential","earning":"thin margin; volume base"}],"source_verified":null,"hero":{"query":"Calakmul, Mexico, Mexico"},"geo":{"lat":18.1057,"lng":-89.8117}}'::jsonb, 17),
  ('campeche-city-mexico', '10S', 'Campeche City, Mexico', 'Mexico', 'Campeche City', 'live', 'verified', 'venice', 'Campeche (Campeche City & Calakmul)', '{"romance"}', '{}', '{"essential","comfort","premier"}', null, null, '{"key_facts":null,"safety":{"emergency":"911","advisory_level":"L1","book_enabled":true,"bin":"freely bookable (L1)","air_access_verified":true,"air_notes":"CPE direct from Mexico City (Aeromexico/Mexicana); Merida MID ~2.5 hr drive as wide-body gateway","advisory_source":"https://travel.state.gov/en/international-travel/travel-advisories/mexico.html","advisory_updated":"2026-05-29","health":["bottled water","heat/sun at ruins & malecon","dengue in rainy season"],"evac":"Merida tertiary care; US medevac (Miami/Houston) for critical trauma"},"timing":{"peak":"Nov-Mar (dry, cool; Dec-Feb sweet spot)","inflection":"early autumn demand build; Carnaval late-Feb micro-peak","fire_date":"mid-to-late September (curve-start minus 1-2 wks); +2nd fire ~2 wks pre-Carnaval","green_season":"Jun-Oct (rainy, hotter, value)","attach":"Merida / Yucatan circuit (~2.5 hr)"},"jewels":[{"name":"Walled centro — pastel streets & eight bastions","si_tag":"CLT","tier":"essential","commission_path":"guided walking tour + boutique-hotel room commission (wall free)","source":"https://whc.unesco.org/en/list/895/","timing":"Nov-Mar","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"culture","when":"Nov-Mar","commission":"guided walking tour + boutique-hotel room commission (wall free)"},{"name":"Puerta de Tierra sound-and-light show","si_tag":"CLT","tier":"essential","commission_path":"bundle into guided evening; ticket non-commissionable pass-through","source":"https://campechecity.com/best-time-to-visit-campeche/","timing":"Nov-Mar","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"culture","when":"Nov-Mar","commission":"bundle into guided evening; ticket non-commissionable pass-through"},{"name":"Fuerte de San Miguel — Museo Arqueológico de Campeche","si_tag":"CLT","tier":"essential","commission_path":"guided half-day + transfer margin; entry non-commissionable","source":"https://www.lonelyplanet.com/mexico/yucatan-peninsula/campeche/attractions/museo-arqueologico-de-campeche-fuerte-de-san-miguel/","timing":"Nov-Mar","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"culture","when":"Nov-Mar","commission":"guided half-day + transfer margin; entry non-commissionable"},{"name":"Edzná Maya ruins (52 km SE)","si_tag":"CLT","tier":"comfort","commission_path":"guided archaeology day tour (DMC/affiliate) + site fee pass-through","source":"https://www.themayanruinswebsite.com/edzna.html","timing":"year-round","timing_type":"ALWAYS-ON","si":"culture","when":"year-round","commission":"guided archaeology day tour (DMC/affiliate) + site fee pass-through"},{"name":"Xtacumbilxunaán caves (near Bolonchén)","si_tag":"CLT","tier":"comfort","commission_path":"guided day tour (commissionable) + entry pass-through","source":"https://www.lonelyplanet.com/mexico/attractions/grutas-de-xtacumbilxunaan/","timing":"Nov-Mar","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"culture","when":"Nov-Mar","commission":"guided day tour (commissionable) + entry pass-through"},{"name":"Isla Aguada / Isla del Carmen dolphin encounter","si_tag":"romance","tier":"comfort","commission_path":"licensed sanctuary boat tour via affiliate (GetYourGuide/Civitatis) or DMC","source":"https://en-yucatan.com/campeche/isla-aguada/","timing":"Nov-Mar","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"Open-water small-boat operation, sun exposure, weather turns Guided only Confirm life vests on board and worn, weather-check the launch, no touching/chasing dolphins, motion-sickness prep","si":"romance","blurb":"Open-water small-boat operation, sun exposure, weather turns Guided only Confirm life vests on board and worn, weather-check the launch, no touching/chasing dolphins, motion-sickness prep","when":"Nov-Mar","commission":"licensed sanctuary boat tour via affiliate (GetYourGuide/Civitatis) or DMC"},{"name":"The Malecón at sunset (7 km Gulf-front)","si_tag":"romance","tier":"essential","commission_path":"free amenity selling boutique-hotel package","source":"https://www.lonelyplanet.com/mexico/yucatan-peninsula/campeche/","timing":"year-round","timing_type":"ALWAYS-ON","si":"romance","when":"year-round","commission":"free amenity selling boutique-hotel package"},{"name":"Candlelit colonial-courtyard dining","si_tag":"romance","tier":"premier","commission_path":"hotel F&B + room commission","source":"https://www.marriott.com/en-us/hotels/cpehl-hacienda-puerta-campeche-a-luxury-collection-hotel-campeche/overview/","timing":"Nov-Mar","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"romance","when":"Nov-Mar","commission":"hotel F&B + room commission"},{"name":"Pan de cazón (state dish)","si_tag":"CUL","tier":"essential","commission_path":"guided food walk / cooking class (tour affiliate)","source":"https://mexiconewsdaily.com/lifestyle/food/state-by-plate-campeches-pan-de-cazon/","timing":"Nov-Mar","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"Campechano cuisine is one of Mexico''s most distinct regional tables","si":"culinary","blurb":"Campechano cuisine is one of Mexico''s most distinct regional tables","when":"Nov-Mar","commission":"guided food walk / cooking class (tour affiliate)"},{"name":"Pámpano en escabeche & coctel campechano","si_tag":"CUL","tier":"essential","commission_path":"curated dining list + food tour / market visit","source":"https://www.mexicotravelandleisure.com/blog/campeche-food-guide/","timing":"Nov-Mar","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"culinary","when":"Nov-Mar","commission":"curated dining list + food tour / market visit"},{"name":"Calakmul gateway (own dossier)","si_tag":"CLT","tier":"premier","commission_path":"multi-day DMC program from Campeche City","source":"https://whc.unesco.org/en/list/895/","timing":"Nov-Mar","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"the deep-jungle Maya megacity + biosphere is a long day/overnight from Campeche City and should not be collapsed into this file","si":"culture","blurb":"the deep-jungle Maya megacity + biosphere is a long day/overnight from Campeche City and should not be collapsed into this file","when":"Nov-Mar","commission":"multi-day DMC program from Campeche City"}],"faq":[{"q":"Is Campeche City safe right now?","a":"Yes — it is among the safest places in Mexico. Campeche is one of only two states (with Yucatán) at US State Dept Level 1 \"Exercise Normal Precautions,\" with no travel restrictions on US government personnel and violent-crime rates among the country''s lowest; the walled centro is walkable day and night. Take normal urban precautions.","source":"travel.state.gov, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"What is there to see in the walled city?","a":"The UNESCO centro itself: a 17th-century wall (1686–1704), eight bastions, a checkerboard grid and 1,000+ colonial buildings painted ochre, coral and mint — walk Calle 59 at golden hour. At night, the Puerta de Tierra sound-and-light show projects four centuries of pirate history onto the Land Gate for about US$5.","source":"whc.unesco.org, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"culture"},{"q":"Is Edzná worth a day trip from Campeche?","a":"Yes — it is the region''s under-visited Maya highlight. Edzná, 52 km southeast, is a major Maya capital whose five-story pyramid rises ~40 m and blends Puuc, Chenes and Petén styles, with a rare ancient hydraulic canal system and a fraction of Chichén Itzá''s crowds. Go at the 8 AM opening to beat the heat.","source":"themayanruinswebsite.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"culture"},{"q":"Is Campeche good for a couple''s trip?","a":"Yes, as a slow, characterful pause. Dinner in a restored-hacienda courtyard (La Guardia at Hacienda Puerta Campeche), a rooftop pool at an 18th-century mansion, and the peninsula''s best sunset along the 7-km malecón make it a honeymoon-adjacent \"second city,\" most often paired with Mérida (~2.5 hr) as a 2–3 night add-on.","source":"lonelyplanet.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"romance"},{"q":"What should I eat in Campeche?","a":"Start with pan de cazón — the state dish of layered tortillas, black beans, shredded dogfish and tomato-habanero sauce. Add pámpano en escabeche (colonial-era pompano in bitter-orange escabeche) and the coctel campechano seafood cocktail, with Gulf catch landed the same morning.","source":"mexiconewsdaily.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"culinary"},{"q":"What''s the real risk to plan for in Campeche?","a":"Heat and thin flight schedules, not crime. The exposed ruins at Edzná and the treeless malecón are hot at midday — hat, high SPF, water and early site visits. Campeche''s own airport (CPE) is thinly served, so most travelers fly into Mérida (MID) and drive ~2.5 hr; drink bottled water only and use repellent for dengue in the rainy season (Jun–Oct).","source":"climatestotravel.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"safety"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"Campeche City, Mexico — The Walled UNESCO Pastel Port | TravelWell.World","search_language":"es-MX","local_keywords":["qué hacer en Campeche","ciudad amurallada Campeche","Edzná zona arqueológica","hoteles boutique centro histórico Campeche","avistamiento de delfines Isla Aguada","pan de cazón Campeche","Carnaval de Campeche fechas"],"long_tail_en":["is Campeche City Mexico safe","things to do in Campeche walled city","Edzná ruins day trip from Campeche","Isla Aguada dolphin tour Campeche","best boutique hotels Campeche historic center"],"hreflang":["en","es-MX"],"jsonld_type":"TouristDestination","author_byline":"By David McCallister — commercial pilot, 56 countries","freshness":"2026-07-07","primary_keyword":"Campeche City"},"booking":null,"si_checklist_25":null,"sis_present":[{"si":"romance","status":"live"}],"ultra":[{"property":"Hacienda Puerta Campeche, a Luxury Collection Hotel","brand":"Marriott — Luxury Collection","rooms":14,"positioning":"Restored 16th-c. haciendas; the destination''s true luxury ceiling","earning":"Marriott commissionable; Luxury Collection eligible for Marriott STARS/Luxury consortia — verify FHR/amenity status at booking","mor":"hotel-direct commission","tier":"$$$$"},{"property":"Casa Don Gustavo Boutique Hotel","rooms":10,"positioning":"Restored 18th-c. mansion, rooftop pool, pedestrian center","earning":"Independent — direct / bedbank / consortia","mor":"hotel-direct or platform","tier":"$$$"},{"property":"Hotel H177","positioning":"Boutique centro property, Calle 59","earning":"Independent boutique; direct / affiliate","mor":"hotel-direct or platform","tier":"comfort"}],"source_verified":null,"hero":{"query":"Campeche City, Mexico, Mexico"},"geo":{"lat":19.845,"lng":-90.523}}'::jsonb, 18),
  ('cancun-mexico', '10S', 'Cancún', 'Mexico', '*If it''s the gateway where a barrier reef meets', 'live', 'verified', 'tropicalBeach', 'Quintana Roo (Cancún & Riviera Maya)', '{"tropical","adventure","diveglobal","ocean"}', '{"tropical"}', '{"essential","comfort"}', null, 'anchor', '{"key_facts":["Sits on the Mesoamerican Barrier Reef, world''s 2nd-longest coral reef system","MUSA underwater museum: 470+ statues, 3.5-8 m, divable and snorkelable","World''s largest whale-shark aggregation offshore mid-May to mid-Sept (snorkel-only)","Best overall window Jan-Mar (clearest water, lowest sargassum)","Gateway hub for cenotes, Chichen Itza/Tulum, Isla Mujeres and Contoy"],"safety":{"emergency":"911","hospital":"Galenia + Hospiten Cancún (verify trauma status); hyperbaric via SSS Cancún / Cozumel","advisory_level":"L2","malaria":"none in QR tourist zones (verify); dengue precautions","yellow_fever":"none required"},"timing":{"peak":"Dec-Apr (dry, lowest sargassum, highest price/crowds)","shoulder":"late Apr-Jun & Nov (~30-40% off, good weather)","green":"Jul-Oct (hurricane/rain, 40-60% below peak Sep-Oct)","booking_lead":"~3-4 months for Dec-Apr peak & spring break; 2-3 months off-peak","off_season_specials":"~30-40% off May-Jun & Nov shoulder; 40-60% off Sep-Oct green trough","event_peaks":["Spring Break (Mar)","whale-shark run mid-May-mid-Sept peak Jun-Aug","winter holidays late Dec"],"campaign_start":"market Dec-Apr peak by ~September; push whale-shark green-season from ~March"},"jewels":[{"name":"MUSA Underwater Museum","si_tag":"diveglobal","status":"future","hook":"470+ submerged sculptures, divable by OW divers and snorkelers","bookable_category":"dive/snorkel/glass-bottom tour","commission_path":"local dive-op/DMC → Viator/GYG affiliate","tier":"comfort","source":"https://www.bluewaterdivetravel.com/scuba-musa-isla-mujeres-cancun","timing":"year-round","timing_type":"ALWAYS-ON","si":"diveglobal","blurb":"470+ submerged sculptures, divable by OW divers and snorkelers","when":"year-round","commission":"local dive-op/DMC → Viator/GYG affiliate"},{"name":"Whale-shark aggregation run","si_tag":"ocean","status":"future","hook":"snorkel the world''s largest whale-shark gathering, Jun-Aug peak","bookable_category":"boat snorkel excursion","commission_path":"DMC/operator → OTA affiliate","tier":"comfort","source":"https://www.islandlifemexico.com/cancun-snorkeling-diving-guide/","si":"ocean","blurb":"snorkel the world''s largest whale-shark gathering, Jun-Aug peak","commission":"DMC/operator → OTA affiliate"},{"name":"Route of the Cenotes","si_tag":"globaladv","status":"live","hook":"jungle-road cenote circuit for swim/dive/zipline","bookable_category":"day tour + entry","commission_path":"DMC → OTA (entry = pass-through)","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.islandlifemexico.com/cancun-snorkeling-diving-guide/","timing":"Dec-Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"adventure","blurb":"jungle-road cenote circuit for swim/dive/zipline","when":"Dec-Apr","commission":"DMC → OTA (entry = pass-through)"},{"name":"Turtle-nesting programs (May-Sept)","si_tag":"globaladv","status":"live","hook":"green/hawksbill/loggerhead nesting + resort release programs","bookable_category":"eco/resort activity","commission_path":"resort/DMC (often pass-through)","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.islandlifemexico.com/cancun-snorkeling-diving-guide/","si":"adventure","blurb":"green/hawksbill/loggerhead nesting + resort release programs","commission":"resort/DMC (often pass-through)"},{"name":"South Hotel Zone / Playa Mujeres (sargassum-protected)","si_tag":"tropical","status":"live","hook":"cleaner beach stretches in a heavy sargassum year","bookable_category":"hotel + transfer","commission_path":"all-inclusive portal → Amstar transfer → OTA","tier":"comfort","source":"https://www.howisthesargassum.com/blog/sargassum-june-2026-update","timing":"Dec-Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"tropical","blurb":"cleaner beach stretches in a heavy sargassum year","when":"Dec-Apr","commission":"all-inclusive portal → Amstar transfer → OTA"}],"faq":[{"q":"Is Cancún safe right now?","a":"Yes — freely bookable. Quintana Roo carries a US State Dept Level 2 \"Exercise Increased Caution\" (dated 2026-05-29) for crime and terrorism — the standard caution for most of Mexico''s resort states — so take normal precautions in the tourist zones.","source":"travel.state.gov","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"What health risks should I actually plan for in Cancún?","a":"Water, mosquitoes, hurricanes and sargassum — not violent crime. Drink bottled/purified water; use repellent for dengue (no malaria in Quintana Roo tourist zones); hurricane season runs June–November with September riskiest; and sargassum peaks around July in 2026.","source":"travel.state.gov","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"Will sargassum ruin the beaches in 2026?","a":"It''s a real risk in 2026 — plan location, don''t cancel. 2026 is tracking as one of the worst sargassum years on record, often peaking around July in the Riviera Maya; north Cancún and Playa Mujeres are among the more protected stretches, and Jan–March runs lowest on sargassum.","source":"howisthesargassum.com","si_tag":"tropical"},{"q":"When and how can I swim with whale sharks?","a":"Mid-May to mid-September, peaking June–August, on a snorkel-only boat excursion off Isla Mujeres/Holbox — the world''s largest whale-shark aggregation. It''s a green-season spike inside the low-price window, so rooms are cheaper then; life-vest, no-touch, follow-the-guide.","source":"islandlifemexico.com","si_tag":"ocean"},{"q":"Can beginners dive MUSA and the reef?","a":"Yes — MUSA is one of the most accessible dives anywhere. The 470+ statues sit 3.5–8 m down, shallow enough for Open Water divers, snorkelers and glass-bottom boats; no-fly-after-diving is 18–24 hours and these are shallow (≤9 m) day dives.","source":"bluewaterdivetravel.com","si_tag":"diveglobal"},{"q":"Is Cancún good for an all-inclusive honeymoon, and where''s the top end?","a":"Yes — it''s a honeymoon engine. The Hotel Zone is dense all-inclusive inventory; the one true ultra address in Cancún proper is NIZUC (Punta Nizuc, ~15 min from the airport), with the deepest luxury bench just down-corridor in Mayakoba/Maroma (Rosewood, Banyan Tree, Maroma/Belmond).","source":"virtuoso.com","si_tag":"tropical"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"Cancún, Mexico: Reef, MUSA & Whale-Shark Gateway","meta_description":"Cancún sits on the world''s second-longest reef — dive MUSA, snorkel the whale-shark run, base for cenotes and Maya ruins. Best time, safety, and how to book.","slug":"cancun-mexico","primary_keyword":"Cancún diving and snorkeling","long_tail":["Cancún MUSA underwater museum","Cancún whale shark tour season","best time to visit Cancún","Cancún all-inclusive honeymoon","Cancún cenote day trip"],"search_language":"EN primary + ES-MX; page answers real ES queries restated (not machine-translated)","local_keywords":["mejor época para viajar a Cancún","buceo MUSA Cancún","tour tiburón ballena Cancún","qué hacer en Cancún cenotes","Cancún todo incluido luna de miel","temporada de sargazo Cancún","villas de lujo Riviera Maya"],"hreflang":["en","es-MX","x-default:en"],"jsonld_type":"TouristDestination","author_byline":"By David McCallister — commercial pilot, 56 countries","content_freshness":"2026-07-04"},"booking":{"bin":"freely_bookable","level":"L2","codes":[],"consent_flow":false,"note":"Quintana Roo/Mexico US L2 (Exercise Increased Caution) - freely bookable; MXN currency, USD widely accepted"},"si_checklist_25":{"run_date":"2026-07-31","hits":9,"misses":13,"disregarded":3,"note":"Canonical 25-SI list; sports limited to participant; spectator/prosports/compsports disregarded"},"sis_present":[{"si":"tropical","name":"tropical","status":"live"},{"si":"globaladv","name":"adventure","status":"live"},{"si":"diveglobal","name":"diveglobal","status":"future"},{"si":"ocean","name":"ocean","status":"future"}],"ultra":[{"name":"NIZUC Resort & Spa","why_ultra":"only true in-Cancún ultra enclave (Punta Nizuc), 274 suites/villas facing the reef","earning":"agent/consortium on application via host + Virtuoso","virtuoso_value_add":"Virtuoso member — free upgrades + amenities","mor":"safe (commissionable-rack / Virtuoso)"},{"name":"Rosewood Mayakoba","why_ultra":"boutique ~130 lagoon/beach suites, private pools + butler, on mangrove canals","earning":"agent/consortium on application via host + Virtuoso","virtuoso_value_add":"Virtuoso member","mor":"safe (commissionable-rack)"},{"name":"Banyan Tree Mayakoba","why_ultra":"all-villa private-pool privacy inside Mayakoba","earning":"agent/consortium on application via host + Virtuoso","virtuoso_value_add":"Virtuoso member","mor":"safe (commissionable-rack)"},{"name":"Fairmont Mayakoba","why_ultra":"full-amenity luxury tier of the Mayakoba four","earning":"agent/consortium on application via host","virtuoso_value_add":"verify (reported NOT Virtuoso; check Accor ALL/other)","mor":"safe (commissionable-rack)"},{"name":"Chablé Maroma","why_ultra":"wellness-forward design ultra, private beach, Jorge Vallejo dining","earning":"agent/consortium on application via host + Virtuoso","virtuoso_value_add":"verify present","mor":"safe (commissionable-rack)"},{"name":"Maroma, A Belmond Hotel","why_ultra":"legendary private-beach ultra, Belmond/LVMH tier","earning":"agent/consortium on application via host + Virtuoso","virtuoso_value_add":"Belmond typically Virtuoso — verify","mor":"safe (commissionable-rack)"},{"name":"La Casa de la Playa (by Xcaret)","why_ultra":"Xcaret''s top-tier ultra all-inclusive, adults/couples + eco-park access","earning":"agent/consortium via Xcaret trade / host on application","virtuoso_value_add":"verify","mor":"safe (commissionable-rack)"}],"source_verified":"2026-07-04","hero":{"query":"Cancún, Mexico"},"geo":{"lat":21.1619,"lng":-86.8515}}'::jsonb, 19),
  ('careyes-mexico', '10S', 'Careyes (Costa Careyes)', 'Mexico', 'Careyes Mexico', 'live', 'verified', 'luxuryPool', 'Jalisco (Puerto Vallarta & Guadalajara)', '{"ultra","romance","ocean"}', '{}', '{"premier","luxury","ultra"}', null, null, '{"key_facts":["Founded 1968 by Gian Franco Brignone; 48-room beach hotel, 36 casitas, ~50 villas + clifftop castles with moat-like infinity pools","Villas privately owned, many rent fully staffed with private cook + daily housekeeping","Polo late-Nov->end-Apr (Agua Alta Cup at Easter, Chinese New Year tournament); Ondalinda x Careyes Nov 12-15 2026","Hosted Heidi Klum & Seal wedding; Tom Ford, Naomi Campbell, Uma Thurman have vacationed","Between PVR and Manzanillo (ZLO ~1.5-hr drive); private charters to Chamela strip CHM31 ~15 min / Chalacatepec ~40 min; Cuixmala & Las Alamandas have own airstrips"],"safety":{"emergency":"911","hospital":"remote enclave; serious cases route to Manzanillo (~1.5 hr) or Puerto Vallarta (~2-4 hr); private airstrips serve medical evac; carry travel-medical + air-evac insurance","advisory_level":"L3","book_enabled":false,"tourist_zone_carveout":"none (private resort enclave; not a named carve-out)","air_access_verified":"private airstrip (Careyes/Cuixmala) + Manzanillo ZLO - flag for founder review","founder_flag":"gated resort enclaves with private airstrips - candidate ''resort-airstrip private-access'' clean-pass class; per gate test content-only until founder rules; LUX ultra moat","malaria":"low - mosquito avoidance (not prophylaxis) for Jalisco coastal lowlands below 1,000 m","dengue":"circulates (peak May-Nov) - daytime repellent","water":"bottled/purified (staffed villas provide)","hurricane":"May-Nov - trip insurance for summer/fall","remote":"minimal public services outside enclave; do NOT drive secondary roads after dark (advisory warning)","road_transfer":"PVR/Manzanillo transfers pass through non-carve-out southern Jalisco - the hold reason; private-air arrival is the founder-flag workaround","dive":"nearest hyperbaric chambers Puerto Vallarta & Manzanillo (1.5-4 hr) - conservative profiles, DAN insurance, strict no-fly interval"},"timing":{"peak":"Nov-Apr (dry season, polo/Ondalinda/celebrity winter season, holiday villa demand, humpbacks Dec-Mar)","shoulder":"May & late Oct (warm, quieter, between festivals)","green":"Jul-Oct (hot/humid, emerald hills, hurricane window May-Nov, softest villa availability)","event_peak":"polo late-Nov->end-Apr (Agua Alta Cup at Easter, Chinese New Year tournament); Ondalinda x Careyes Nov 12-15 2026","booking_window_lead_time":"staffed ultra villas for Christmas-New Year/winter polo/Ondalinda book 6-12 months ahead, contracted direct on application; binding constraint is villa availability, not flights","out_of_season_fill_the_beds":"green season (Jul-Oct) villa buyouts at softer rates as private-family estate stays (turtle nesting Cuixmala) - the ''secret season''","holiday_event_peaks":"Christmas-New Year (ultra premium), Semana Santa/Easter (Agua Alta Cup polo), Chinese New Year (polo+gala), Ondalinda (mid-Nov)","campaign_start_trigger":"content-only - no campaign; if founder rules private-air carve-out, open winter/polo/Ondalinda villa campaigns in spring for following Nov-Apr peak (6-12-mo villa lead)","sources":["https://www.ondalinda.com/festivals/careyes/","https://careyes.com/","https://mexiconewsdaily.com/travel/an-insiders-guide-to-the-perfect-weekend-in-costalegre/"]},"jewels":[{"name":"Careyes clifftop Castles","si_tag":"Luxury / Ultra-Luxury","status":"future","tier":"ultra","bookable":"Careyes reservations / villa specialist","commission_path":"on application","source":"https://careyes.com/","timing":"year-round","timing_type":"ALWAYS-ON","hook":"candy-colored castles with moat-like infinity pools cantilevered over the Pacific — the signature Careyes image","si":"ultra","blurb":"candy-colored castles with moat-like infinity pools cantilevered over the Pacific — the signature Careyes image","when":"year-round","commission":"on application"},{"name":"Cuixmala (Casa Cuixmala suites / hillside villas)","si_tag":"Luxury / Ultra-Luxury","status":"future","tier":"ultra","bookable":"Cuixmala direct / luxury DMC","commission_path":"on application","source":"https://www.luxurylatinamerica.com/mexico/cuixmala.html","timing":"Nov-Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"Goldsmith''s 25,000-acre biosphere estate — zebras, nesting turtles, private airstrip, total seclusion","si":"ultra","blurb":"Goldsmith''s 25,000-acre biosphere estate — zebras, nesting turtles, private airstrip, total seclusion","when":"Nov-Apr","commission":"on application"},{"name":"Las Alamandas","si_tag":"Luxury / Ultra-Luxury","status":"future","tier":"ultra","bookable":"Las Alamandas direct / DMC","commission_path":"on application","source":"https://www.alamandas.com/","timing":"Nov-Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"18 suites across 8 villas, plus 16% VAT / 3% room tax / 14% service. On application","si":"ultra","blurb":"18 suites across 8 villas, plus 16% VAT / 3% room tax / 14% service. On application","when":"Nov-Apr","commission":"on application"},{"name":"Careyes staffed-villa honeymoon","si_tag":"Romance & Honeymoons","status":"future","tier":"ultra","bookable":"Careyes reservations / villa specialist","commission_path":"on application","source":"https://careyes.com/","timing":"Nov-Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"private staffed villa/casita with cook, cliff-and-cove privacy — a celebrity-wedding coast","si":"romance","blurb":"private staffed villa/casita with cook, cliff-and-cove privacy — a celebrity-wedding coast","when":"Nov-Apr","commission":"on application"},{"name":"El Careyes Club & Residences","si_tag":"Romance & Honeymoons","status":"future","tier":"luxury","bookable":"Careyes reservations","commission_path":"on application","source":"https://careyes.com/","timing":"Nov-Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"beachfront club stay for couples wanting hotel-style service inside the enclave","si":"romance","blurb":"beachfront club stay for couples wanting hotel-style service inside the enclave","when":"Nov-Apr","commission":"on application"},{"name":"Careyes polo - Agua Alta Cup (Easter)","si_tag":"Ocean Adventures","status":"future","tier":"premier","bookable":"Careyes events / villa package","commission_path":"on application","source":"https://www.ondalinda.com/festivals/careyes/","timing":"Nov-Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"the enclave''s signature spectacle, played Easter week; Chinese New Year tournament too","si":"ocean","blurb":"the enclave''s signature spectacle, played Easter week; Chinese New Year tournament too","when":"Nov-Apr","commission":"on application"},{"name":"Sailing + winter humpback coast","si_tag":"Ocean Adventures","status":"future","tier":"luxury","bookable":"charter / villa concierge (content-only)","commission_path":"operator (content-only)","source":"https://www.costalegre.ca/","hook":"sailing off the coves; humpbacks migrate Dec–Mar offshore","si":"ocean","blurb":"sailing off the coves; humpbacks migrate Dec–Mar offshore","commission":"operator (content-only)"}],"faq":[{"q":"Can I book Careyes through TravelWell right now?","a":"No — Careyes is content-only today. Jalisco sits at US State Dept Level 3 \"Reconsider Travel\" (May 29, 2026), and the advisory''s only named no-restriction carve-outs are the Guadalajara Metro area, Puerto Vallarta, Chapala and Ajijic — four zones that do not include Careyes. Failing that named-carve-out gate sets book_enabled=FALSE.","source":"travel.state.gov, 2026-05-29","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"What''s the real risk to plan for at Careyes?","a":"The road transfer, not the enclave itself. Ground transfers from Puerto Vallarta or Manzanillo run through non-carve-out southern Jalisco, and the advisory warns specifically against secondary highways after dark — this is the hold reason. The enclave is also remote: serious medical cases route ~1.5 hr to Manzanillo or 2–4 hr to Puerto Vallarta, so air-evac insurance is essential.","source":"travel.state.gov / careyes.com, 2026-07-04","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"What makes Careyes so exclusive?","a":"It is a genuinely private, family-owned ultra node — not a resort. Founded in 1968, it pairs clifftop castles and ~50 staffed villas with two adjacent Goldsmith estates: Cuixmala, a ~25,000-acre biosphere reserve with its own airstrip, and Las Alamandas, an 18-suite gated boutique. All three have private airstrips — the crux of a possible future \"arrive-by-private-air\" clean pass.","source":"luxurylatinamerica.com / careyes.com, 2026-07-04","si_tag":"ultra"},{"q":"Is Careyes good for a honeymoon or wedding?","a":"Yes — it is one of Mexico''s most cinematic private-wedding coasts. Heidi Klum and Seal married here, and the product is a fully staffed villa or casita with a private cook and total cliff-and-cove privacy, plus El Careyes Club & Residences for hotel-style service. Peak is the dry Nov–Apr season, and villas for that window contract 6–12 months ahead.","source":"careyes.com / aol.com, 2026-07-04","si_tag":"romance"},{"q":"When is polo season and the Ondalinda festival?","a":"Professional polo runs late November to the end of April, with the marquee Agua Alta Cup played Easter week and a Chinese New Year tournament; the Ondalinda x Careyes festival is dated Nov 12–15, 2026. Winter also brings humpbacks offshore (Dec–Mar). Staffed-villa demand for these dates books 6–12 months out.","source":"ondalinda.com, 2026-07-04","si_tag":"ocean"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"Careyes Mexico: Clifftop Castles, Polo & the Costalegre Ultra Coast","meta_description":"Careyes — Gian Franco Brignone''s 1968 private ultra enclave on Jalisco''s Costalegre: clifftop castles, staffed villas, polo, sailing, Ondalinda, plus Cuixmala & Las Alamandas.","slug":"careyes-mexico","primary_keyword":"Careyes Mexico","long_tail":["Careyes villas rent","Careyes clifftop castles","Careyes polo Agua Alta Cup","Ondalinda Careyes 2026","Cuixmala vs Careyes vs Las Alamandas","Careyes private airstrip access"],"search_language":["en","es-MX"],"local_keywords":["Careyes Mexico","villas Careyes renta","castillos Careyes","polo Careyes Copa Agua Alta","Ondalinda Careyes 2026","Cuixmala reserva","Las Alamandas Costalegre"],"hreflang":["en","es-MX"],"jsonld_type":"TouristDestination","author_byline":"By David McCallister — commercial pilot, 56 countries","content_freshness":"2026-07-04"},"booking":null,"si_checklist_25":null,"sis_present":[{"si":"Luxury / Ultra-Luxury","status":"future"},{"si":"romance","status":"future"},{"si":"ocean","status":"future"}],"ultra":[{"name":"Cuixmala","posture":"Goldsmith ~25,000-acre private biosphere estate; suites/villas/casitas; zebras+turtles; private airstrip","price_tier":"ultra","earning":"on application / luxury DMC (Journey Mexico) / villa specialist","virtuoso_value_add":"likely via luxury-DMC channel - verify at contract","mor":"no net-rate resale","book_gated":"founder carve-out decision (private-airstrip clean-pass class)","source":"https://www.luxurylatinamerica.com/mexico/cuixmala.html"},{"name":"Careyes (Casitas / Castles)","posture":"Brignone 1968 clifftop enclave; hotel + casitas + ~50 villas + moat-pool castles; polo/sailing/Ondalinda; private-air via Chamela CHM31 ~15 min","price_tier":"ultra","earning":"on application / villa specialist","virtuoso_value_add":"verify at contract","mor":"no net-rate resale","book_gated":"founder carve-out decision","source":"https://careyes.com/"},{"name":"Las Alamandas","posture":"Isabel Goldsmith 18-suite gated ultra-boutique on private bay; own 3,300-ft asphalt airstrip (currently unavailable - use Chamela strip 15 min)","price_tier":"ultra","earning":"on application / DMC","virtuoso_value_add":"likely via luxury-DMC channel - verify","mor":"no net-rate resale","book_gated":"founder carve-out decision","source":"https://www.alamandas.com/"},{"name":"El Careyes (Club & Residences)","posture":"beachfront club/residences arm of the Careyes enclave","price_tier":"luxury","earning":"on application","virtuoso_value_add":"verify at contract","mor":"no net-rate resale","book_gated":"founder carve-out decision","source":"https://careyes.com/"}],"source_verified":"2026-07-04","hero":{"query":"Careyes (Costa Careyes), Mexico"},"geo":{"lat":19.4,"lng":-105.03}}'::jsonb, 20)
