tion timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"three colored ridges reached by a short, far-less-punishing walk; the smart pick for travelers who want the palette without the 5,200 m gut-check","si":"expedition","blurb":"three colored ridges reached by a short, far-less-punishing walk; the smart pick for travelers who want the palette without the 5,200 m gut-check","when":"May–August","commission":"DMC / activity affiliate"},{"name":"Humantay Lake (~4,200 m)","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"comfort","commission_path":"DMC / activity affiliate","source":"https://www.salkantaytrekking.com/traditional/cusco/humantay-lake-full-day/","hook":"a turquoise glacial lake under Salkantay''s snows; a demanding half-day climb from Soraypampa","si":"expedition","blurb":"a turquoise glacial lake under Salkantay''s snows; a demanding half-day climb from Soraypampa","commission":"DMC / activity affiliate"},{"name":"Salkantay Pass trek (~4,650 m)","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"premier","commission_path":"DMC multi-day trek","source":"https://www.salkantaytrekking.com/trekking-in-peru/cusco/salkantay-rainbow-mountain-trek-7d/","timing":"May–August","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"the high alternative to the Inca Trail, often chained to Machu Picchu; multi-day, guided","si":"expedition","blurb":"the high alternative to the Inca Trail, often chained to Machu Picchu; multi-day, guided","when":"May–August","commission":"DMC multi-day trek"},{"name":"San Blas artisan barrio, Cusco","si_tag":"culture","tier":"essential","commission_path":"DMC city tour / affiliate","source":"https://www.salkantaytrekking.com/blog/maras-and-moray-sacred-valley-guide/","timing":"May–August","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"the steep bohemian quarter of workshops, silversmiths and cafés above the Plaza. Free to wander; monetizes through walking tours + boutique retail","si":"culture","blurb":"the steep bohemian quarter of workshops, silversmiths and cafés above the Plaza. Free to wander; monetizes through walking tours + boutique retail","when":"May–August","commission":"DMC city tour / affiliate"},{"name":"Sacsayhuamán + Q''enqo","si_tag":"culture","tier":"comfort","commission_path":"DMC guided; Boleto Turístico entry","source":"https://turismoliberty.pe/en/cusco-tourist-ticket-2026/","timing":"May–August","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"the cyclopean fortress-temple above Cusco and the nearby carved ritual site; both on the Boleto Turístico Circuit I","si":"culture","blurb":"the cyclopean fortress-temple above Cusco and the nearby carved ritual site; both on the Boleto Turístico Circuit I","when":"May–August","commission":"DMC guided; Boleto Turístico entry"},{"name":"Pisac market + ruins","si_tag":"culture","tier":"comfort","commission_path":"DMC circuit; Boleto Turístico III","source":"https://www.salkantaytrekking.com/blog/maras-and-moray-sacred-valley-guide/","timing":"year-round","timing_type":"ALWAYS-ON","hook":"the classic Andean textile/craft market beneath dramatic terraced ruins and an ancient cliff cemetery","si":"culture","blurb":"the classic Andean textile/craft market beneath dramatic terraced ruins and an ancient cliff cemetery","when":"year-round","commission":"DMC circuit; Boleto Turístico III"},{"name":"Ollantaytambo living-Inca town","si_tag":"culture","tier":"comfort","commission_path":"DMC circuit + rail; Boleto Turístico III","source":"https://www.machupicchureservations.org/tour/sacred-valley-tour-full-day-2/","timing":"May–August","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"one of the last inhabited Inca settlements, streets still fed by working 500-year-old canals","si":"culture","blurb":"one of the last inhabited Inca settlements, streets still fed by working 500-year-old canals","when":"May–August","commission":"DMC circuit + rail; Boleto Turístico III"},{"name":"Maras salt pans + Moray terraces","si_tag":"culture","tier":"comfort","commission_path":"DMC circuit; Boleto Turístico III (Moray)","source":"https://www.salkantaytrekking.com/blog/maras-and-moray-sacred-valley-guide/","timing":"May–August","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"4,500+ hand-worked salt pools fed by a pre-Inca spring, and the Inca''s circular \"agricultural laboratory\" of microclimate terraces. Iconic photography, deep story","si":"culture","blurb":"4,500+ hand-worked salt pools fed by a pre-Inca spring, and the Inca''s circular \"agricultural laboratory\" of microclimate terraces. Iconic photography, deep story","when":"May–August","commission":"DMC circuit; Boleto Turístico III (Moray)"},{"name":"Chinchero weaving village","si_tag":"culture","tier":"essential","commission_path":"DMC circuit + artisan retail; Boleto Turístico III","source":"https://www.salkantaytrekking.com/blog/maras-and-moray-sacred-valley-guide/","timing":"May–August","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"the \"birthplace of the rainbow,\" high-plateau town with a Textile Interpretation Center where women demonstrate natural-dye alpaca weaving","si":"culture","blurb":"the \"birthplace of the rainbow,\" high-plateau town with a Textile Interpretation Center where women demonstrate natural-dye alpaca weaving","when":"May–August","commission":"DMC circuit + artisan retail; Boleto Turístico III"},{"name":"Cusco Cathedral + Qorikancha","si_tag":"culture","tier":"comfort","commission_path":"DMC city tour; separate admissions","source":"https://turismoliberty.pe/en/cusco-tourist-ticket-2026/","timing":"year-round","timing_type":"ALWAYS-ON","hook":"the colonial cathedral on the Plaza de Armas and the Inca Temple of the Sun whose gold-clad walls the Spanish built Santo Domingo atop","si":"culture","blurb":"the colonial cathedral on the Plaza de Armas and the Inca Temple of the Sun whose gold-clad walls the Spanish built Santo Domingo atop","when":"year-round","commission":"DMC city tour; separate admissions"},{"name":"San Pedro Market, Cusco","si_tag":"culture","tier":"essential","commission_path":"DMC food/market tour","source":"https://www.salkantaytrekking.com/blog/maras-and-moray-sacred-valley-guide/","timing":"May–August","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"the working city market: produce, cheeses, juices, textiles, street food; the sensory anchor of a food-focused day","si":"culture","blurb":"the working city market: produce, cheeses, juices, textiles, street food; the sensory anchor of a food-focused day","when":"May–August","commission":"DMC food/market tour"},{"name":"Pisco + Andean cuisine chef''s-table","si_tag":"RHN / Culinary","tier":"premier","commission_path":"DMC private dining / lodge F&B","source":"https://luxurylatinamerica.com/blog/2024/12/10/stay-in-the-sacred-valley/","timing":"May–August","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"the high-Andes ingredient story at chef''s-table and tasting-menu level, paired with pisco. Sacred Valley luxe lodges and Cusco''s fine-dining scene carry this","si":"RHN / Culinary","blurb":"the high-Andes ingredient story at chef''s-table and tasting-menu level, paired with pisco. Sacred Valley luxe lodges and Cusco''s fine-dining scene carry this","when":"May–August","commission":"DMC private dining / lodge F&B"}],"faq":[{"q":"Do you need to acclimatize before Rainbow Mountain?","a":"Yes — acclimatize 1–2 days minimum in Cusco or the valley before any high hike, and never climb Rainbow Mountain on your first or second day. It matters because more than a third of travelers to Cusco feel altitude sickness, the summit sits at ~5,200 m (roughly 11% effective oxygen), and the core risk is acute mountain sickness, not terrain. Go guided — reputable operators carry oxygen, manage pace and pull travelers who deteriorate.","source":"turismoliberty.pe, Accessed 2026-07-07","si_tag":"expedition"},{"q":"What does the Cusco Tourist Ticket cover?","a":"The integral Boleto Turístico costs S/130 (~$35), is valid 10 days across 16 sites, and is cash-only in soles with no online option. Note what it does not cover: Machu Picchu, Qorikancha, the Cathedral, Rainbow Mountain and Humantay all require separate admission, so budget those as pass-through costs on top.","source":"turismoliberty.pe, Accessed 2026-07-07","si_tag":"culture"},{"q":"Which are the best luxury lodges in the Sacred Valley and Cusco?","a":"The honeymoon spine runs from Cusco''s Belmond Palacio Nazarenas (55 oxygen-enriched all-suites) and Belmond Monasterio (a 16th-century monastery, 117 rooms) out to the valley''s explora Valle Sagrado, Sol y Luna (Relais & Châteaux) and Tambo del Inka — the Luxury Collection resort with its own private rail station to Machu Picchu.","source":"belmond.com, Accessed 2026-07-07","si_tag":"romance"},{"q":"When do you need to book for Inti Raymi and peak season?","a":"Book 3–4 months out — by late March, ideally February — for June–August and Inti Raymi trips, because capacity, not price, is what runs out. Inti Raymi (the Festival of the Sun) falls on June 24 and sells the city out months ahead, and Machu Picchu tickets, trains and hotels are capacity-capped in peak season.","source":"perurail.com, Accessed 2026-07-07","si_tag":"expedition"},{"q":"Is Cusco safe to visit right now given Peru''s Level 2 advisory?","a":"Yes — it is freely bookable. Peru''s national Level 2 (Exercise Increased Caution) is driven by conditions concentrated elsewhere, notably the Level 4 VRAEM narco-corridor and periodic urban unrest. Cusco city, the Sacred Valley, the Inca Trail and Machu Picchu are explicitly carved clean by State and permitted for U.S. government personnel. Do verify strikes/paros live before travel, as they can suspend trains and site access.","source":"travel.state.gov, Accessed 2026-07-07","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"What''s the real risk in Cusco — is it altitude?","a":"Yes — altitude outranks crime by a wide margin. Cusco sits at ~3,400 m and Rainbow Mountain at ~5,200 m, and more than a third of travelers feel altitude sickness (soroche), some moderate-to-severe. Acclimatize 1–2 days before any high hike, ascend gradually, hydrate, use coca, and discuss prophylactic acetazolamide (Diamox) with a physician; the emergency number is 105.","source":"turismoliberty.pe, Accessed 2026-07-07","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"Is Rainbow Mountain dangerous?","a":"The danger is altitude, not the walk. At ~5,200 m the core risk is acute mountain sickness, so guided is strongly preferred — reputable operators carry oxygen, manage pace and pull travelers who deteriorate — and the non-negotiable rule is to acclimatize 1–2 days first. Travelers who want the color without the 5,200 m gut-check can take Palccoyo, the gentler-altitude \"rainbow\" alternative.","source":"altitude-peru.com, Accessed 2026-07-07","si_tag":"safety"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"Cusco & the Sacred Valley, Peru — Travel Guide, Treks, Luxury Lodges & Altitude Tips | TravelWell.World","jsonld_type":"TouristDestination","author_byline":"By David McCallister — commercial pilot, 56 countries","freshness":"2026-07-07","search_language":"es-PE","local_keywords":["qué hacer en Cusco","Valle Sagrado tour","Montaña de 7 Colores","boleto turístico Cusco 2026","mal de altura Cusco soroche","Laguna Humantay","Inti Raymi 24 de junio","Maras Moray salineras","Ollantaytambo qué ver"],"hreflang":["en","es-PE"],"primary_keyword":"Cusco & the Sacred Valley"},"booking":null,"si_checklist_25":null,"sis_present":[{"si":"culture","status":"live"}],"ultra":[{"name":"Belmond Palacio Nazarenas","location":"Cusco","earning":"Virtuoso preferred; agency AoR + VIP amenities","mor":"agency/hotel","tier":"$$$$"},{"name":"Belmond Monasterio","location":"Cusco","earning":"Virtuoso preferred; agency AoR","mor":"agency/hotel","tier":"$$$$"},{"name":"Belmond Río Sagrado","location":"Sacred Valley","earning":"Virtuoso/Belmond preferred; agency AoR","mor":"agency/hotel","tier":"$$$$"},{"name":"JW Marriott El Convento Cusco","location":"Cusco","earning":"Marriott Luxury/STARS; agency AoR + Bonvoy","mor":"agency/hotel","tier":"$$$$"},{"name":"Inkaterra La Casona","location":"Cusco","earning":"Relais & Châteaux/Virtuoso; agency AoR","mor":"agency/hotel","tier":"$$$$"},{"name":"explora Valle Sagrado","location":"Sacred Valley","earning":"Virtuoso; agency AoR","mor":"agency/hotel","tier":"$$$$"},{"name":"Sol y Luna","location":"Sacred Valley","earning":"Relais & Châteaux/Virtuoso; agency AoR","mor":"agency/hotel","tier":"$$$$"},{"name":"Tambo del Inka, a Luxury Collection Resort & Spa","location":"Sacred Valley (Urubamba)","earning":"Marriott Luxury/STARS; agency AoR + Bonvoy","mor":"agency/hotel","tier":"$$$$"}],"source_verified":null,"hero":{"query":"Cusco & the Sacred Valley, Peru, Peru"},"geo":{"lat":-13.5319,"lng":-71.9675}}'::jsonb, 32),
  ('east-cape-mexico', '10S', 'East Cape (Cabo del Este)', 'Mexico', 'The wild Sea-of-Cortez side of Cabo **TravelWell', 'live', 'verified', 'tropicalBeach', 'Baja California Sur (Los Cabos & La Paz)', '{"romance","expedition","diveglobal","ocean"}', '{}', '{"essential","comfort","premier","luxury","ultra"}', null, null, '{"key_facts":["Costa Palmas spans 1,500 acres with 3 km of swimmable Sea-of-Cortez beach, ~45 min from SJD airport (Source: costapalmas.com, 2026-07-04)","Prime sportfishing May–early Nov: blue/black/striped marlin, sailfish, dorado, wahoo, yellowfin tuna (Source: marinalife.com, 2026-07-04)","El Norte wind peaks Dec–Mar at 15–25 kt; Los Barriles is a top-tier kite/windsurf beach (Source: middlecasa.com, 2026-07-04)","Whales present in Baja waters late Dec–early Apr, offshore in the Sea of Cortez (Source: oceanicsociety.org, 2026-07-04)","Cabo Pulmo NP: 7,111-ha no-take reserve ~30 km from Los Barriles; +462% fish abundance by 2010 (Source: en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cabo_Pulmo_National_Park, 2026-07-04)"],"safety":{"emergency":"911","hospital":"Hospital H+ Los Cabos (Km 24.5, 624-104-9300, ~45+ min) or La Paz (~2.5 hr); local East Cape Health Center Los Barriles is daytime clinic only","advisory_level":"L2","malaria":"none","yellow_fever":"not required"},"timing":{"peak":"Nov–Apr (dry, whales late Dec–early Apr, El Norte wind Dec–Mar)","shoulder":"May & Oct–Nov (fishing ramp, pre/post-heat)","green":"Jul–Sep (hottest + hurricane window Jun–Nov; peak billfish/dorado)","booking_lead":"6–12 mo Costa Palmas ultra & holiday villas; 1–3 mo peak fishing charters (verify)","off_season_specials":"green-season fishing packages + villa value windows; Van Wormer customizable group packages 2–200","event_peaks":"Christmas/New Year & Easter (Costa Palmas holiday premium); Lord of the Wind kite/windsurf showdown (January, Los Barriles)","campaign_start":"Aug–Sep for Nov–Apr Romance/whale peak; Mar–Apr for May–Nov fishing; Sep–Oct for kite/windsurf"},"jewels":[{"name":"Costa Palmas beachfront (3 km swimmable sea)","si_tag":"Romance & Honeymoons","status":"live","hook":"rare swimmable Cabo-side beach with two ultra brands on one estate","bookable_category":"resort/villa","tier":"ultra","commission_path":"Four Seasons Preferred Partner + host-Virtuoso; MoR villa","source":"https://costapalmas.com/ + Accessed 2026-07-04","si":"romance","blurb":"rare swimmable Cabo-side beach with two ultra brands on one estate","commission":"Four Seasons Preferred Partner + host-Virtuoso; MoR villa","accessed":"2026-07-04"},{"name":"Casa Blake (Marina Village)","si_tag":"Romance & Honeymoons","status":"live","hook":"boutique hotel + condo pied-à-terre at the marina heart","bookable_category":"hotel/residence","tier":"luxury","commission_path":"agency/host","source":"https://costapalmas.com/overview/ + Accessed 2026-07-04","si":"romance","blurb":"boutique hotel + condo pied-à-terre at the marina heart","commission":"agency/host","accessed":"2026-07-04"},{"name":"Sea-of-Cortez whale season","si_tag":"Global Expedition Adventures","status":"live","hook":"offshore gray/humpback/blue/fin whales in one of Earth''s richest whale seas","bookable_category":"day tour / private charter","tier":"comfort","commission_path":"activity affiliate (~4–8%) or DMC","source":"https://www.oceanicsociety.org/travel-ideas/best-whale-watching-in-baja-the-complete-guide/ + Accessed 2026-07-04","si":"expedition","blurb":"offshore gray/humpback/blue/fin whales in one of Earth''s richest whale seas","commission":"activity affiliate (~4–8%) or DMC","accessed":"2026-07-04"},{"name":"East Cape billfish grounds","si_tag":"Ocean Adventures","status":"future","hook":"legendary marlin/dorado/wahoo/tuna variety, billfish year-round","bookable_category":"fishing charter","tier":"premier","commission_path":"DMC/Van Wormer fishing desk","source":"https://www.marinalife.com/articles/fishing-mexicos-east-cape + Accessed 2026-07-04","timing":"Nov–Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"ocean","blurb":"legendary marlin/dorado/wahoo/tuna variety, billfish year-round","when":"Nov–Apr","commission":"DMC/Van Wormer fishing desk","accessed":"2026-07-04"},{"name":"Roosterfish inshore","si_tag":"Ocean Adventures","status":"future","hook":"iconic catch-and-release inshore fight; global rooster hotspot","bookable_category":"panga charter","tier":"essential","commission_path":"local operator","source":"https://www.marinalife.com/articles/fishing-mexicos-east-cape + Accessed 2026-07-04","timing":"Nov–Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"ocean","blurb":"iconic catch-and-release inshore fight; global rooster hotspot","when":"Nov–Apr","commission":"local operator","accessed":"2026-07-04"},{"name":"Los Barriles kite/windsurf (El Norte)","si_tag":"Ocean Adventures","status":"future","hook":"15–25 kt afternoons Dec–Mar; Lord of the Wind in January","bookable_category":"school/camp + hotel package","tier":"comfort","commission_path":"activity affiliate / lesson package","source":"https://middlecasa.com/why-los-barriles-is-mexicos-winter-mecca-for-kitesurfers/ + Accessed 2026-07-04","si":"ocean","blurb":"15–25 kt afternoons Dec–Mar; Lord of the Wind in January","commission":"activity affiliate / lesson package","accessed":"2026-07-04"},{"name":"Cabo Pulmo reef (cross-link, own dossier)","si_tag":"Dive Globally","status":"future","hook":"20,000-yr-old richest reef on NA west coast; +462% fish abundance recovery","bookable_category":"local dive op (lottery sites)","tier":"comfort","commission_path":"local dive op; NP fees non-commissionable","source":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cabo_Pulmo_National_Park + Accessed 2026-07-04","timing":"Nov–Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"diveglobal","blurb":"20,000-yr-old richest reef on NA west coast; +462% fish abundance recovery","when":"Nov–Apr","commission":"local dive op; NP fees non-commissionable","accessed":"2026-07-04"}],"faq":[{"q":"Is the East Cape a good honeymoon base?","a":"Yes — it holds two of Mexico''s most serious luxury resorts on one estate. Costa Palmas fronts a rare swimmable Cabo-side beach (3 km) with the Four Seasons and Amanvari, 45 minutes from SJD, so couples get calm water plus branded ultra away from the corridor crowds.","source":"costapalmas.com, 2026-07-04","si_tag":"romance"},{"q":"When can I see whales in the Sea of Cortez here?","a":"Late December to early April, with the blue-whale peak Feb–Apr. Gray, humpback, blue and fin whales all pass offshore, on day tours or private charters out of the East Cape — one of Earth''s richest whale seas.","source":"oceanicsociety.org, 2026-07-04","si_tag":"expedition"},{"q":"When is the fishing and the wind best on the East Cape?","a":"Two opposite seasons: billfish and dorado peak May to early November in glass-calm water, while the El Norte wind turns Los Barriles into a 15–25 kt kite and windsurf arena Dec–March. Pick the season for the sport you came for.","source":"marinalife.com / middlecasa.com, 2026-07-04","si_tag":"ocean"},{"q":"Is the East Cape safe, and how remote is it really?","a":"It is freely bookable — Baja California Sur is US State Dept Level 2 (May 29, 2026) and one of Mexico''s safer states — but genuinely remote. Nearest full trauma care is Hospital H+ Los Cabos ~45+ minutes away and the Los Barriles clinic is daytime-only, so brief offshore-fishing and remote-beach clients on the medevac reality.","source":"travel.state.gov, 2026-05-29 / eastcapehealthcenter.org, 2026-07-04","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"Is diving reachable from here, and is it safe?","a":"Yes — Cabo Pulmo, the reef that recovered 462%, sits ~30 km south (its own dossier), a no-take/no-glove reserve with lottery-governed top sites. The nearest recompression chamber is Hospital H+ Los Cabos (~45+ min), so plan conservative profiles and observe 18–24 h no-fly before flying.","source":"en.wikipedia.org / hmasloscabos.mx, 2026-07-04","si_tag":"diveglobal"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"East Cape Baja (Costa Palmas) Travel Guide — Fishing, Whales & Ultra-Luxury | TravelWell.World","meta_description":"The wild Sea-of-Cortez side of Cabo: Costa Palmas ultra (Four Seasons + Amanvari), world-class marlin/dorado sportfishing, Los Barriles kite season, whales Dec–Apr, and the Cabo Pulmo reef.","slug":"east-cape-mexico","primary_keywords":["East Cape Baja","Costa Palmas","East Cape sportfishing","Los Barriles kiteboarding","Four Seasons Los Cabos Costa Palmas"],"long_tail":["best time to fish East Cape Baja","whale watching Sea of Cortez December April","Amanvari Aman Costa Palmas","luxury villa rental East Cape","Cabo Pulmo diving from Los Barriles"],"search_language":"es-MX","local_keywords":["Cabo del Este Baja","Costa Palmas Los Cabos","pesca deportiva Cabo del Este","kitesurf Los Barriles El Norte","avistamiento de ballenas Mar de Cortés","buceo Cabo Pulmo","villas de lujo Cabo del Este"],"hreflang":["en","es-MX"],"jsonld_type":"TouristDestination","author_byline":"By David McCallister — commercial pilot, 56 countries","content_freshness":"2026-07-04"},"booking":null,"si_checklist_25":null,"sis_present":[{"si":"romance","status":"live"},{"si":"expedition","status":"live"},{"si":"diveglobal","status":"future"},{"si":"ocean","status":"future"}],"ultra":[{"name":"Four Seasons Resort Los Cabos at Costa Palmas","why_ultra":"141-room flagship + beachfront residences on private 1,500-acre estate, swimmable beach, RTJ II golf","earning":"Four Seasons Preferred Partner or via host-Virtuoso (never fabricate %)","virtuoso_value_add":"daily breakfast for two, ~$100 resort credit, upgrade priority, early check-in/late check-out, ~$495 airport transfer, VIP recognition","mor":"MoR on villa rentals"},{"name":"Amanvari (Aman, Costa Palmas)","why_ultra":"first Aman in Mexico; intimate 18-key + 4–7BR Aman Residences (13k–20k sq ft), Aman Spa, private beach","earning":"on application / via host-Aman-preferred (never fabricate %)","virtuoso_value_add":"per Aman preferred-partner program","mor":"MoR on residences"},{"name":"Costa Palmas Marina & residences","why_ultra":"only Four Seasons + Aman branded marina in Los Cabos; superyacht harbor up to ~250 ft; Marina Village","earning":"real-estate/rental via host","virtuoso_value_add":"n/a (property/marina)","mor":"MoR"}],"source_verified":"2026-07-04","hero":{"query":"East Cape (Cabo del Este), Mexico"},"geo":{"lat":23.68,"lng":-109.7,"note":"approx Los Barriles / La Ribera–Costa Palmas corridor"}}'::jsonb, 33),
  ('el-calafate-argentina', '10S', 'El Calafate & Argentine Patagonia', 'Argentina', 'El Calafate & Argentine Patagonia', 'live', 'verified', 'mountainValley', 'Patagonia & The Lakes', '{"expedition"}', '{}', '{"essential","comfort","premier","luxury","ultra"}', null, null, '{"key_facts":null,"safety":{"emergency":"911","emergency_secondary":["101 police","107 ambulance (SAME)","100 fire","0800 999 5000 tourist line"],"advisory_level":"L1","book_enabled":true,"bin":"freely bookable (L1)","consent_flow":false,"air_access_verified":true,"air_access_note":"El Calafate FTE via Buenos Aires AEP (domestic) / EZE (international); Ushuaia USH; Bariloche BRC","remote_flag":true,"trauma_note":"El Calafate clinic stabilises; serious trauma evac to Buenos Aires by air; El Chaltén/Ushuaia more remote","exposure_headline":"Patagonian wind (80-100 km/h) + rapid weather change; ice-trek requires crampons + certified guide (guided-only); Fitz Roy day-hikes weather-exposed","water_potable":true,"mandatory_insurance":"Non-resident travel medical insurance required since 2025-07-01 (treatment, hospitalisation, repatriation, evacuation)"},"timing":{"peak":"Dec-Feb (Jan busiest)","shoulder":["Oct-Nov","Mar-Apr"],"winter_counterseason":"Bariloche ski Jun-Oct (best Aug-early Sep)","big_ice_season":"mid-Sep to end-Apr","antarctica_season":"Nov-Mar","booking_lead":{"peak_lodges_and_treks":"6-12 months","nearby_multiday_treks":"5-6 months","antarctica":"12+ months"},"fire_date":"curve-start minus 1-2 weeks; practically 6-12 months ahead for peak, ~2 weeks before visible curve for shoulder"},"jewels":[{"name":"Perito Moreno boardwalks + Big Ice trek","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"comfort","commission_path":"activity affiliate + DMC land package","source":"https://calafate.tours/en/perito-moreno-glacier/","hook":"the marquee. Free-flowing boardwalk viewing up to guided Big Ice","si":"expedition","blurb":"the marquee. Free-flowing boardwalk viewing up to guided Big Ice","commission":"activity affiliate + DMC land package"},{"name":"Upsala & Spegazzini glacier cruise (Lago Argentino)","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"premier","commission_path":"activity affiliate + DMC","source":"https://gopatagonic.com/excursion-to-upsala-and-spegazzini-glaciers/","timing":"Dec-Feb","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"sail past icebergs to walls most visitors never reach; often paired with Estancia Cristina. ~11-hr day","si":"expedition","blurb":"sail past icebergs to walls most visitors never reach; often paired with Estancia Cristina. ~11-hr day","when":"Dec-Feb","commission":"activity affiliate + DMC"},{"name":"Estancia Cristina","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"premier","commission_path":"DMC / estancia direct + activity affiliate","source":"https://www.southernexplorations.com/extension/argentina/el-calafate/estancia-cristina/","timing":"Dec-Feb","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"historic end-of-the-world ranch reached only by boat across Lago Argentino; 4×4 to Upsala viewpoint or horseback to Pearson Lagoon","si":"expedition","blurb":"historic end-of-the-world ranch reached only by boat across Lago Argentino; 4×4 to Upsala viewpoint or horseback to Pearson Lagoon","when":"Dec-Feb","commission":"DMC / estancia direct + activity affiliate"},{"name":"Glaciarium ice museum","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"essential","commission_path":"activity affiliate","source":"https://calafate.tours/en/perito-moreno-glacier/","timing":"year-round","timing_type":"ALWAYS-ON","hook":"the polished, all-weather glaciology museum + ice bar just outside El Calafate; perfect weather-buffer day","si":"expedition","blurb":"the polished, all-weather glaciology museum + ice bar just outside El Calafate; perfect weather-buffer day","when":"year-round","commission":"activity affiliate"},{"name":"Laguna de los Tres / Fitz Roy day trek","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"essential","commission_path":"self-guided (park-free) or guided via DMC/outfitter","source":"https://www.patagoniahub.travel/en/hiking-trails/el-chalten-laguna-de-los-tres","si":"expedition","commission":"self-guided (park-free) or guided via DMC/outfitter"},{"name":"Laguna Torre (Cerro Torre)","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"essential","commission_path":"self-guided or guided","source":"https://www.machupicchu.org/el-chalten-hiking-guide-2026-fitz-roy-cerro-torre-trails.htm","timing":"Dec-Feb","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"flatter, ~18 km round-trip to a glacial lagoon under Cerro Torre; the accessible counterpart to Los Tres","si":"expedition","blurb":"flatter, ~18 km round-trip to a glacial lagoon under Cerro Torre; the accessible counterpart to Los Tres","when":"Dec-Feb","commission":"self-guided or guided"},{"name":"Loma del Pliegue Tumbado","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"comfort","commission_path":"guided recommended","source":"https://www.machupicchu.org/el-chalten-hiking-guide-2026-fitz-roy-cerro-torre-trails.htm","timing":"Dec-Feb","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"the panoramic ridge that puts both Fitz Roy and Cerro Torre in one frame; less crowded, more climb","si":"expedition","blurb":"the panoramic ridge that puts both Fitz Roy and Cerro Torre in one frame; less crowded, more climb","when":"Dec-Feb","commission":"guided recommended"},{"name":"Tierra del Fuego National Park","si_tag":"Expedition Cruise","tier":"essential","commission_path":"activity affiliate + DMC","source":"https://www.secretatlas.com/handbook/antarctica/ushuaia","timing":"Dec-Feb","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"sub-Antarctic forest, peat bogs, the \"end of the world\" train, day hikes from Ushuaia","si":"Expedition Cruise","blurb":"sub-Antarctic forest, peat bogs, the \"end of the world\" train, day hikes from Ushuaia","when":"Dec-Feb","commission":"activity affiliate + DMC"},{"name":"Beagle Channel cruise","si_tag":"Expedition Cruise","tier":"comfort","commission_path":"activity affiliate","source":"https://www.machupicchu.org/beagle-channel-cruise-2026-from-ushuaia-penguins-sea-lions-lighthouses.htm","timing":"Dec-Feb","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"penguin colonies, sea-lion islands, Les Éclaireurs lighthouse; day cruise before or after an Antarctic embarkation","si":"Expedition Cruise","blurb":"penguin colonies, sea-lion islands, Les Éclaireurs lighthouse; day cruise before or after an Antarctic embarkation","when":"Dec-Feb","commission":"activity affiliate"},{"name":"Ushuaia Antarctica embarkation","si_tag":"Expedition Cruise","tier":"ultra","commission_path":"own-CLIA / Fora cruise lane","source":"https://www.adventure-life.com/argentina/ushuaia","timing":"Dec-Feb","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"the reason Ushuaia exists on the luxury map; see Ultra","si":"Expedition Cruise","blurb":"the reason Ushuaia exists on the luxury map; see Ultra","when":"Dec-Feb","commission":"own-CLIA / Fora cruise lane"},{"name":"Circuito Chico (Bariloche)","si_tag":"SKI/Lake District","tier":"essential","commission_path":"DMC / self-drive + activity affiliate","source":"https://www.daytours4u.com/en/travel-guide/discover-cerro-catedral-complete-guide-skiing-bariloche-beyond/1759","timing":"Dec-Feb","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"the ~60 km scenic drive along Nahuel Huapi past Llao Llao and the Andean lake overlooks; year-round","si":"SKI/Lake District","blurb":"the ~60 km scenic drive along Nahuel Huapi past Llao Llao and the Andean lake overlooks; year-round","when":"Dec-Feb","commission":"DMC / self-drive + activity affiliate"},{"name":"Cerro Catedral (ski)","si_tag":"ski","tier":"comfort","commission_path":"ski-package DMC + affiliate","source":"https://powderquest.com/ski-resorts/argentina/catedral/","timing":"Dec-Feb","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"largest ski resort in South America, 70+ pistes, austral-winter counter-season","si":"ski","blurb":"largest ski resort in South America, 70+ pistes, austral-winter counter-season","when":"Dec-Feb","commission":"ski-package DMC + affiliate"},{"name":"Ruta 40 overland","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"comfort","commission_path":"car-rental affiliate + DMC self-drive","source":"https://www.interpatagonia.com/elcalafate/famous-estancia-cristina.html","si":"expedition","commission":"car-rental affiliate + DMC self-drive"}],"faq":[{"q":"Can you walk on the Perito Moreno glacier?","a":"Yes, but only with a certified guide. \"Mini-trekking\" straps you into crampons for ~1.5 hours on the ice (a ~10-hour day with boat and transfer), and \"Big Ice\" gives ~3.5 hours deep among crevasses and ice caves (ages ~18–50, high difficulty). Ice-trekking is guided-only — crevasses and moulins are lethal — and Big Ice runs mid-September to end of April.","source":"calafate.tours, Accessed 2026-07-07","si_tag":"expedition"},{"q":"When is the best time to visit El Calafate and Patagonia?","a":"Austral summer — December through February, with January the busiest — is peak, with longest daylight (up to ~17 hours) and 8–17 °C. Best conditions run Oct–Mar, and October and March give the best weather-to-crowds ratio; peak lodges and treks sell out 6–12 months ahead, so book early.","source":"worldlyadventurer.com, Accessed 2026-07-07","si_tag":"expedition"},{"q":"Which honeymoon lodge should we book in Patagonia?","a":"EOLO – Patagonia''s Spirit is the flagship: a 17-room Relais & Châteaux full-board lodge on a 4,000-ha estate on the Perito Moreno road, sold via the Virtuoso/Fora advisor lane. It sells out 6–12 months ahead for peak summer, so fire early — the \"Perito Moreno at sunrise, fire-warmed lodge, no cell signal\" pitch writes itself.","source":"relaischateaux.com, Accessed 2026-07-07","si_tag":"romance"},{"q":"Where do Antarctica cruises leave from?","a":"Ushuaia — the Southern Hemisphere''s Antarctica embarkation port, and the last town before the Drake Passage. Every peninsula voyage that matters departs Nov–Mar, with entry expedition fares ~US$12,000–15,000+ per person (luxury far higher) on Ponant, Silversea, Lindblad and Aurora; the best cabins go 12+ months out.","source":"silversea.com, Accessed 2026-07-07","si_tag":"expedition-cruise"},{"q":"Can you ski near El Calafate?","a":"Not at El Calafate itself, but Bariloche flips to ski season while El Calafate quiets in winter. Cerro Catedral — the largest ski resort in South America, with 70+ pistes — runs Jun–Sep, with the best snow Aug–early September. This is the region''s counter-season revenue lane.","source":"powderquest.com, Accessed 2026-07-07","si_tag":"ski"},{"q":"Is El Calafate and Patagonia safe right now?","a":"Yes. Argentina is at U.S. State Department Level 1 \"Exercise Normal Precautions,\" the safest tier alongside Japan and Germany, and the only elevated crime node is Rosario (city L2), far from Patagonia. The genuine risk profile here is environmental, not criminal — weather, wind, cold, and distance from advanced medical care.","source":"travel.state.gov, Accessed 2026-07-07","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"What''s the real risk to plan for in Patagonia?","a":"Wind and weather. Patagonian wind and rapid weather change are the number-one hazard — gusts funnel through the Fitz Roy cirque at 80–100 km/h even on \"calm\" days, and wind chill at the lagoon can push effective temps below freezing. El Calafate, El Chaltén and Ushuaia are remote, so serious trauma routes to Buenos Aires by air; build buffer days and carry insurance covering repatriation and evacuation.","source":"machupicchu.org, Accessed 2026-07-07","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"Is glacier ice-trekking dangerous?","a":"It is a hard rule, not a preference: guided-only. Both mini-trekking (~1.5 hr) and Big Ice (~3.5 hr, crevasses and ice caves, ages ~18–50) require crampons and a certified glacier guide, because crevasses and moulins are lethal — ice-trekking should never be presented as self-guided under any circumstance.","source":"calafate.tours, Accessed 2026-07-07","si_tag":"safety"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"El Calafate & Argentine Patagonia: Perito Moreno Glacier, Fitz Roy Trekking & Ushuaia | TravelWell.World","meta_description":"Walk on the Perito Moreno glacier, trek Fitz Roy from El Chaltén, sail Lago Argentino, and sail from Ushuaia to Antarctica — the complete guide to Argentine Patagonia.","long_tail_en":["perito moreno glacier ice trekking","el calafate to el chalten itinerary","fitz roy laguna de los tres day hike","best time to visit patagonia argentina","ushuaia antarctica cruise gateway","estancia cristina upsala glacier cruise"],"search_language":"es-AR","local_keywords":["qué hacer en El Calafate","Perito Moreno minitrekking","El Chaltén trekking Fitz Roy","cruceros Lago Argentino Upsala","Ushuaia crucero Antártida","esquí Bariloche Cerro Catedral"],"hreflang":["en","es-AR"],"jsonld_type":"TouristDestination","author_byline":"By David McCallister — commercial pilot, 56 countries","freshness":"2026-07-07","primary_keyword":"El Calafate & Argentine Patagonia"},"booking":null,"si_checklist_25":null,"sis_present":[{"si":"expedition","status":"live"}],"ultra":[{"name":"EOLO – Patagonia''s Spirit","type":"Relais & Châteaux lodge","location":"El Calafate","earning":"Virtuoso/Fora advisor commission + amenities","mor":"AOR/advisor","tier":"ultra"},{"name":"Design Suites Calafate","type":"design upscale","location":"El Calafate","earning":"advisor/DMC commission","mor":"AOR/DMC","tier":"luxury"},{"name":"Los Ponchos","type":"boutique estancia-style","location":"El Calafate","earning":"advisor/DMC commission","mor":"AOR/DMC","tier":"luxury"},{"name":"Explora El Chaltén","type":"all-inclusive lodge","location":"Los Huemules / El Chaltén","earning":"advisor commission (all-in nightly)","mor":"AOR/advisor","tier":"ultra"},{"name":"Llao Llao","type":"grand hotel","location":"Bariloche","earning":"Virtuoso/Fora advisor commission","mor":"AOR/advisor","tier":"ultra"},{"name":"Arakur Ushuaia","type":"ridge-top luxury","location":"Ushuaia","earning":"advisor/DMC commission","mor":"AOR/advisor","tier":"ultra"},{"name":"Antarctica expedition (Ponant/Silversea/Lindblad/Aurora)","type":"expedition cruise","location":"ex-Ushuaia","earning":"own-CLIA / Fora cruise commission","mor":"cruise agency (own-CLIA)","tier":"ultra"}],"source_verified":null,"hero":{"query":"El Calafate & Argentine Patagonia, Argentina"},"geo":{"lat":-50.3379,"lng":-72.2648}}'::jsonb, 34),
  ('ensenada-mexico', '10S', 'Ensenada, Mexico', 'Mexico', 'Wine roads and the cold Pacific **TravelWell', 'live', 'verified', 'tropicalBeach', 'Baja California (Valle de Guadalupe & Ensenada)', '{"tropical","expedition","romance","culinary"}', '{"tropical"}', '{"essential","comfort"}', null, null, '{"key_facts":null,"safety":{"emergency":"911","book_enabled":true,"bin":"BOOK WITH WARNING","consent_flow":{"disclosure_required":true,"renders":"full verbatim live advisory + acknowledgment","wording_status":"hook set only - PENDING compliance-attorney sign-off"},"state_dept_carveout":"Ensenada no-restriction","restricted_away_zone":"Mexicali Valley (sole BC restricted zone; not transited on Ensenada corridor)","trauma_evac":"San Diego, USA (nearest tertiary trauma; ground or air ambulance)","hazards":["Pacific riptides / cold water / heavy surf","rural-road / night-driving caution","bottled water only"],"air_access_verified":true,"air_access_note":"Tijuana (TIJ) via Cross Border Xpress (CBX) from San Diego + ~1.5 hr drive Mex-1D; or drive/shuttle from San Diego ~2 hr; active cruise port (3rd busiest in Mexico)"},"timing":{"peak":["Summer (Jun-Sep)","Fiestas de la Vendimia (late Jul - late Aug)"],"secondary_peak":"Gray-whale migration Dec-Apr (offshore, peak Jan-Mar)","inflection":["Late spring (May-early Jun)","Autumn shoulder (Oct)"],"fire_date":"curve-start minus 1-2 weeks (fire Vendimia ~early Jul; whale season ~early Dec)","baseline":"cruise-day pulse year-round"},"jewels":[{"name":"La Bufadora blowhole + Punta Banda","si_tag":"GEA/Coastal","tier":"essential","commission_path":"GetYourGuide/Viator excursion + DMC transfer (blowhole free)","source":"https://www.bajabound.com/destinations/ensenada/labufadora","timing":"[''Summer '', ''Fiestas de la Vendimia '']","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"GEA/Coastal","when":"[''Summer '', ''Fiestas de la Vendimia '']","commission":"GetYourGuide/Viator excursion + DMC transfer (blowhole free)"},{"name":"Gray-whale migration (offshore Dec-Apr)","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"comfort","commission_path":"licensed whale-watch charter + affiliate","source":"https://www.seakayakadventures.com/blog/top-10-things-you-need-know-about-baja-gray-whale-season","si":"expedition","commission":"licensed whale-watch charter + affiliate"},{"name":"Sportfishing - Todos Santos Bay","si_tag":"GEA/Coastal","tier":"comfort","commission_path":"charter operator commission","source":"https://sergiosfishing.com/whales/","timing":"[''Summer '', ''Fiestas de la Vendimia '']","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"GEA/Coastal","when":"[''Summer '', ''Fiestas de la Vendimia '']","commission":"charter operator commission"},{"name":"Mercado Negro fish market + fish-taco birthplace","si_tag":"culinary","tier":"essential","commission_path":"culinary/market tour affiliate + DMC","source":"https://mexiconewsdaily.com/food/the-mystery-behind-the-invention-of-the-baja-fish-taco/","timing":"year-round","timing_type":"ALWAYS-ON","si":"culinary","when":"year-round","commission":"culinary/market tour affiliate + DMC"},{"name":"La Guerrerense (Sabina Bandera tostadas)","si_tag":"culinary","tier":"essential","commission_path":"Sabina restaurant reservation + food-tour affiliate (cart non-commissionable)","source":"https://guide.michelin.com/us/en/baja-california/ensenada_2059847/restaurant/sabina","timing":"[''Summer '', ''Fiestas de la Vendimia '']","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"culinary","when":"[''Summer '', ''Fiestas de la Vendimia '']","commission":"Sabina restaurant reservation + food-tour affiliate (cart non-commissionable)"},{"name":"Guadalupe/San Quintin oysters + aquaculture","si_tag":"culinary","tier":"comfort","commission_path":"farm-tour experience operator + culinary DMC","source":"https://www.bajacalifornia.travel/en/editorial/you-have-to-try-this-why-san-quintin-oysters-are-bajas-best-kept-secret","timing":"[''Summer '', ''Fiestas de la Vendimia '']","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"culinary","when":"[''Summer '', ''Fiestas de la Vendimia '']","commission":"farm-tour experience operator + culinary DMC"},{"name":"Valle de Guadalupe wine day","si_tag":"Culinary/Romance","tier":"comfort","commission_path":"wine-tour operator + winery reservations + hotel packages","source":"https://www.winetraveler.com/mexico/best-valle-de-guadalupe-wineries/","timing":"[''Summer '', ''Fiestas de la Vendimia '']","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"Drink-and-drive is the 1 fire — unlit rural roads between wineries Driver/guide strongly recommended","si":"Culinary/Romance","blurb":"Drink-and-drive is the 1 fire — unlit rural roads between wineries Driver/guide strongly recommended","when":"[''Summer '', ''Fiestas de la Vendimia '']","commission":"wine-tour operator + winery reservations + hotel packages"},{"name":"Ensenada Malecon + Riviera del Pacifico Cultural Center","si_tag":"Romance/Culture","tier":"essential","commission_path":"city/culture tour affiliate (center entry low/free)","source":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hotel_Riviera_del_Pac%C3%ADfico","timing":"year-round","timing_type":"ALWAYS-ON","si":"Romance/Culture","when":"year-round","commission":"city/culture tour affiliate (center entry low/free)"}],"faq":[{"q":"Is Ensenada safe to visit, and can I book it?","a":"Yes — it is book-enabled with a mandatory consent flow. Baja California carries a US State Dept Level 3 \"Reconsider Travel\" advisory (issued 2026-05-29), but the advisory states the only travel restrictions in the state are in the Mexicali Valley and names Ensenada with no added restriction. Every booking renders the full live advisory first.","source":"travel.state.gov, 2026-05-29","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"What''s the real risk to plan for?","a":"Drink-and-drive on wine roads, and the cold Pacific — not the Mexicali cartel context, which lies far east and is never transited on the Ensenada corridor. Use a driver for any Valle de Guadalupe tasting day, treat the open Pacific as look-don''t-swim (strong riptides, cold water), and route serious trauma north to San Diego.","source":"travel.state.gov, 2026-05-29","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"Where do I eat the famous fish tacos?","a":"Around the Mercado Negro, where they were arguably invented. Ensenada is credited as the birthplace of the modern Baja fish taco (c.1960), and doña Sabina Bandera''s La Guerrerense cart — a 2013 World Street Food Congress medalist and MICHELIN-recognized name — is the must-eat; nearby San Quintín Kumamoto oysters extend the culinary lane.","source":"mexiconewsdaily.com / guide.michelin.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"culinary-—-future"},{"q":"What is La Bufadora and when''s it best?","a":"It''s one of North America''s largest marine geysers, best at high tide. On the Punta Banda peninsula, La Bufadora shoots seawater up to ~100 feet when swell compresses air in a sea cave; entry is free (nominal parking), and winter swells give the biggest spouts. Mind the slippery, unfenced cliff edges.","source":"bajabound.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"expedition"},{"q":"Can I do Valle de Guadalupe as a day trip?","a":"Yes — it''s ~40 minutes northeast, with 250+ wineries and a farm-to-table scene. Book a guided wine day with a driver rather than self-driving, since the rural roads between wineries are the #1 safety fire; the Fiestas de la Vendimia (late Jul–late Aug) is the demand apex and sells out first.","source":"winetraveler.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"romance"},{"q":"Can I see gray whales from Ensenada?","a":"Yes — offshore, December–April, peak January–March. Gray whales pass along the Pacific coast Ensenada→San Quintín on the longest mammal migration on earth; go with a licensed charter (life vests, weather-holds), noting the \"friendly\" lagoon nurseries lie farther south in Baja California Sur.","source":"seakayakadventures.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"expedition"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"Ensenada, Mexico: La Bufadora, Fish Tacos & Valle de Guadalupe Wine Gateway | TravelWell","search_language":"es-MX","local_keywords":["qué hacer en Ensenada","La Bufadora","tacos de pescado Ensenada","tour Valle de Guadalupe desde Ensenada","La Guerrerense tostadas","Mercado Negro Ensenada","ballenas grises Ensenada"],"hreflang":["en","es-MX"],"jsonld_type":"TouristDestination","author_byline":"By David McCallister - commercial pilot, 56 countries","freshness":"2026-07-07"},"booking":null,"si_checklist_25":null,"sis_present":null,"ultra":[{"property":"Banyan Tree Veya Valle de Guadalupe","location":"Valle de Guadalupe (inland cross-ref)","fit":"brand-flag ultra; Amex FHR","mor":"consortia/FHR commission + amenities","tier":"$$$$$"},{"property":"Bruma Wine Resort","location":"Valle de Guadalupe (cross-ref)","fit":"high-design boutique-luxury","mor":"villa-rate/boutique consortia","tier":"$$$$"},{"property":"Encuentro Guadalupe","location":"Valle de Guadalupe (cross-ref)","fit":"design-forward pioneer","mor":"boutique consortia","tier":"$$$$"},{"property":"Hotel Punta Morro","location":"Ensenada coast","fit":"upper-boutique ceiling (in-town best)","mor":"direct/boutique commission","tier":"$$$"}],"source_verified":null,"hero":{"query":"Ensenada, Mexico, Mexico"},"geo":{"lat":31.8667,"lng":-116.5964}}'::jsonb, 35),
  ('espiritu-santo-island-mexico', '10S', 'Espíritu Santo Island', 'Mexico', 'Espíritu Santo island', 'live', 'verified', 'oceanAerial', 'Baja California Sur (Los Cabos & La Paz)', '{"expedition","ocean"}', '{}', '{"comfort","premier","luxury"}', null, null, '{"key_facts":["Uninhabited Sea-of-Cortez island, ~80.8 km2, off La Paz Baja California Sur","UNESCO Biosphere Reserve (1994) + World Heritage Site (2005) + Archipielago Espiritu Santo National Park (2007, ~479.9 km2)","CONANP permit (paper bracelet) required; open sunrise-sunset; permitted capacity managed (~40%)","Los Islotes: 600+ California sea lions, snorkel-only; colony closed Jun 1-Aug 31 (pupping)","NO lodging except permitted 8-tent Camp Cecil (Nov-Apr); day tours ~$100-150 pp, private sail ~$600+/boat"],"safety":{"emergency":"911","hospital":"NONE on-island (uninhabited, no cell service); boat to La Paz then Hospital Salvatierra/ISSSTE/private + air-evac; medical/evac insurance essential","advisory_level":"L2","malaria":"effectively none in Baja California Sur","dengue":"circulates in Mexico - use repellent","water":"carry own bottled/purified water - no services on-island","hurricane":"Jun-Nov - trip insurance for summer/fall","sea_lion":"SNORKEL ONLY, no-touch; Los Islotes closed Jun 1-Aug 31; keep guide distance from territorial bulls; licensed operator required","island_day_use":"NO services, NO cell, permit required, sunrise-sunset only, carry-in/carry-out, capacity managed","dive":"nearest hyperbaric chamber in La Paz (verify); DAN +1-919-684-9111; no-fly 18-24h; dive-within-cert; current on channel/open-water"},"timing":{"peak":"Nov-Apr (dry desert winter, calm seas); rides La Paz whale-shark high season Oct-Apr","shoulder":"May & Sep (warm water, sea lions open, softer demand)","green":"Jun-Aug (summer heat, hurricane window, sea-lion colony closed Jun 1-Aug 31 - beach/snorkel day-trips only)","booking_window_lead_time":"no island hotel; permitted camp beds tiny (Camp Cecil 8 tents, Nov-Apr, 2-night min) - book camps 3-6 months ahead; day tours days-weeks out, peak sea-lion days fill faster","out_of_season_fill_the_beds":"beach/snorkel day tours, San Rafaelito reef (sea-lion substitute during closure), kayak/SUP among cliffs, private sailing charters","holiday_event_peaks":"Christmas-New Year, Semana Santa, sea-lion core Sep-May; Camp Cecil Nov-Apr maps to peak","campaign_start_trigger":"camp/private-sailing campaigns May-Jul (Nov opening + limited beds); sea-lion day-tour campaigns Aug-Sep ahead of fall reopening; summer day-trip value in spring","flag":"sea lions closed Jun 1-Aug 31; summer overlaps hurricane season Jun-Nov; NO lodging except seasonal 8-tent camp","sources":["https://www.thoroughlytravel.com/isla-espiritu-santo/","https://scubaboard.com/community/threads/la-paz-sea-lion-colony-closed-for-snorkel-scuba-june-1-aug-31.621077/","https://www.islands.com/story/resorts/the-glamping-experience-of-isla-espiritu-santo-camp-cecil/"]},"jewels":[{"name":"Los Islotes sea-lion snorkel","si_tag":"Global Expedition Adventures","status":"live","tier":"comfort","bookable":"permitted day tour from La Paz (Sep-May)","commission_path":"local operator + Journey Mexico DMC + Viator affiliate","source":"https://www.goworldtravel.com/snorkeling-sea-lions-sea-of-cortez/","hook":"swim with 600+ California sea lions at one of Mexico''s healthiest colonies","si":"expedition","blurb":"swim with 600+ California sea lions at one of Mexico''s healthiest colonies","commission":"local operator + Journey Mexico DMC + Viator affiliate"},{"name":"Full-day island snorkel + cove landing","si_tag":"Global Expedition Adventures","status":"live","tier":"premier","bookable":"permitted day tour incl. CONANP bracelet","commission_path":"local operator + DMC","source":"https://www.thoroughlytravel.com/isla-espiritu-santo/","hook":"pink-cliff coves, white-sand beaches, reef snorkel on an uninhabited UNESCO island","si":"expedition","blurb":"pink-cliff coves, white-sand beaches, reef snorkel on an uninhabited UNESCO island","commission":"local operator + DMC"},{"name":"Kayak / SUP among the cliffs","si_tag":"Global Expedition Adventures","status":"live","tier":"comfort","bookable":"kayak/SUP eco tour","commission_path":"eco operator (Eco Migrations) + GYG affiliate","source":"https://ecomigrations.com/tour/espiritu-santo-island-sea-lion-snorkeling-paddleboarding-tour/","hook":"paddle the empty coves and sea-lion waters; low-impact, all-ages","si":"expedition","blurb":"paddle the empty coves and sea-lion waters; low-impact, all-ages","commission":"eco operator (Eco Migrations) + GYG affiliate"},{"name":"Overnight glamping (Camp Cecil)","si_tag":"Global Expedition Adventures","status":"live","tier":"luxury","bookable":"TOSEA operator package (Nov-Apr, 2-night min, from ~$375 pp)","commission_path":"TOSEA / host-Virtuoso on application","source":"https://www.islands.com/story/resorts/the-glamping-experience-of-isla-espiritu-santo-camp-cecil/","timing":"Nov-Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"sleep on the island — 8 solar tents, sea lions off the beach, all-inclusive naturalist","si":"expedition","blurb":"sleep on the island — 8 solar tents, sea lions off the beach, all-inclusive naturalist","when":"Nov-Apr","commission":"TOSEA / host-Virtuoso on application"},{"name":"San Rafaelito reef snorkel/dive","si_tag":"Ocean Adventures / Dive Globally","status":"future","tier":"comfort","bookable":"dive/snorkel charter (sea-lion-closure substitute)","commission_path":"dive operator + affiliate","source":"https://scubaboard.com/community/threads/la-paz-sea-lion-colony-closed-for-snorkel-scuba-june-1-aug-31.621077/","hook":"the sea-lion-closure substitute reef; also a fine standalone snorkel","si":"Ocean Adventures / Dive Globally","blurb":"the sea-lion-closure substitute reef; also a fine standalone snorkel","commission":"dive operator + affiliate"}],"faq":[{"q":"When can I snorkel with sea lions at Los Islotes?","a":"September through May — the colony of 600+ California sea lions closes Jun 1–Aug 31 for pupping and mating, when operators substitute the San Rafaelito reef. It''s a snorkel-only, no-touch encounter with a licensed operator, usually on a ~$100–150 full-day island tour.","source":"goworldtravel.com / scubaboard.com, 2026-07-04","si_tag":"expedition"},{"q":"Can I stay overnight on Espíritu Santo?","a":"Only at Camp Cecil, a permitted 8-tent solar camp open Nov–Apr (2-night minimum) — there are no hotels, roads or cell service on this protected, uninhabited UNESCO island. Everyone else visits sunrise-to-sunset by permitted boat and carries everything in and out.","source":"islands.com / thoroughlytravel.com, 2026-07-04","si_tag":"wildlife"},{"q":"How do I visit if the sea lions are closed?","a":"Come for the empty island itself — pink-cliff coves, white-sand beaches, kayak/SUP and the San Rafaelito reef snorkel that substitutes for Los Islotes in summer. Private crewed sailing charters (from ~$600+ per boat) are the calmest way to see it.","source":"thoroughlytravel.com / scubaboard.com, 2026-07-04","si_tag":"ocean"},{"q":"Is Espíritu Santo safe to visit?","a":"Yes — freely bookable. Baja California Sur is US State Dept Level 2 (May 29, 2026) and one of Mexico''s safer states; the real caveat is isolation, not crime.","source":"travel.state.gov, 2026-05-29","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"What''s the real risk on an uninhabited island?","a":"No services, no cell signal and no medical facilities. Any emergency requires a boat back to La Paz, then Hospital Salvatierra or private clinics with air-evac for major trauma — so carry travel medical + evacuation insurance and bring your own water, food and sun protection.","source":"hgejms.gob.mx / thoroughlytravel.com, 2026-07-04","si_tag":"safety"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"Espíritu Santo Island: UNESCO Sea-of-Cortez Guide","meta_description":"Snorkel with sea lions at Los Islotes and land on uninhabited, UNESCO-listed Espíritu Santo from La Paz — permits, seasons (colony closed Jun–Aug) and how to book.","slug":"espiritu-santo-island-mexico","primary_keyword":"Espíritu Santo island","long_tail":["Espiritu Santo tour from La Paz","Los Islotes sea lion snorkel season","Espiritu Santo CONANP permit","Camp Cecil glamping Espiritu Santo","uninhabited island Sea of Cortez"],"search_language":["en","es-MX"],"local_keywords":["Isla Espíritu Santo tour desde La Paz","nadar con lobos marinos Los Islotes","permiso CONANP Isla Espíritu Santo","Parque Nacional Archipiélago Espíritu Santo","campamento Camp Cecil Espíritu Santo","snorkel Mar de Cortés isla deshabitada"],"hreflang":["en","es-MX"],"jsonld_type":"TouristDestination","author_byline":"By David McCallister — commercial pilot, 56 countries","content_freshness":"2026-07-04"},"booking":null,"si_checklist_25":null,"sis_present":[{"si":"expedition","status":"live"},{"si":"Ocean Adventures / Dive Globally","status":"future"}],"ultra":[{"name":"Camp Cecil de la Isla","posture":"only overnight on the UNESCO island; eco-luxe 8-tent solar camp (TOSEA)","price_tier":"ultra","earning":"on application / host-Virtuoso or TOSEA operator terms","virtuoso_value_add":"private full-camp buy-out (8 tents) + naturalist upgrade on application","mor":"no net-rate resale","source":"https://www.islands.com/story/resorts/the-glamping-experience-of-isla-espiritu-santo-camp-cecil/"},{"name":"Private crewed sailing charter (Espiritu Santo)","posture":"ultra way to see the island without lodging (~$600+/boat and up)","price_tier":"ultra","earning":"on application via host / Journey Mexico DMC","virtuoso_value_add":"private naturalist + provisioning on application","mor":"no net-rate resale","source":"https://www.thoroughlytravel.com/isla-espiritu-santo/"}],"source_verified":"2026-07-04","hero":{"query":"Espíritu Santo Island, Mexico"},"geo":{"lat":24.4714,"lng":-110.3325}}'::jsonb, 36)
insert into public.destinations (id, region_code, name, country, line, status, depth, img, sub_region, si, feel, tier_range, price_band, draw_rank, data, position) values
  ('fernando-de-noronha-brazil', '10S', 'Fernando de Noronha, Brazil', 'Brazil', 'Volcanic archipelago, marine sanctuary, dolphin dawn **TravelWell', 'live', 'verified', 'oceanAerial', 'Northeast Beaches & Bahia', '{"liveaboard","tropical","romance","expedition"}', '{"tropical"}', '{"essential","comfort","premier"}', null, null, '{"key_facts":null,"safety":{"emergency":"190","advisory_level":"L2","advisory_why":"mainland urban crime + kidnapping; favelas L4. Archipelago itself is low-risk controlled-access marine park.","book_enabled":true,"bin":"freely bookable (L2)","consent_flow":false,"air_access_verified":true,"air_access":"FEN via Recife (REC) or Natal (NAT) only — Gol/Azul","no_fly_after_diving":"18-24h surface interval before FEN->mainland flight; plan dive-free last day","hyperbaric_chamber_onisland":true,"hyperbaric_note":"chamber adjacent to Hospital Sao Lucas (basic care); serious trauma/complex DCI requires mainland evac (Recife/Natal); weather can delay","remote_flag":true,"ocean_hazards":["strong currents/swell at outer-sea pinnacles & deep sites","riptides (worst Dec-Mar)","equatorial sun"],"protected_no_entry":["Baia dos Golfinhos (dolphin resting bay)"]},"timing":{"dive_calendar":true,"peak_dive":"Aug-Nov (viz apex Sep-Oct)","peak_surf_highseason":"Dec-Mar","inflection":["late July","late November"],"fire_date":"curve-start minus 1-2 weeks (mid-late July for dive peak; mid-late November for Dec-Mar season)","booking_lead":"3-6 months for Dec-Mar (visitor cap + eco-tax + park permit)","offseason_fill":"Apr-Jun (rain hits surface, reef viz stays strong — diver''s value window)"},"jewels":[{"name":"Baia do Sancho","si_tag":"Tropical/Beaches","tier":"comfort","commission_path":"park ticket (pass-through) + commissionable boat/DMC day","source":"https://www.tripadvisor.com/Attraction_Review-g616328-d2391494-Reviews-Baia_do_Sancho-Fernando_de_Noronha_State_of_Pernambuco.html","si":"Tropical/Beaches","commission":"park ticket (pass-through) + commissionable boat/DMC day"},{"name":"Forte Boldro sunset viewpoint","si_tag":"Tropical/Beaches","tier":"essential","commission_path":"guided island tour add-on","source":"https://postcardfromtaylor.com/blog/brazil/noronha-beaches/","timing":"year-round","timing_type":"ALWAYS-ON","si":"Tropical/Beaches","when":"year-round","commission":"guided island tour add-on"},{"name":"Ilha-tour boat trip","si_tag":"Tropical/Beaches","tier":"comfort","commission_path":"commissionable boat operator/DMC","source":"https://www.natalriograndedonorte.com/fernando-de-noronha-diving-and-snorkeling/","si":"Tropical/Beaches","commission":"commissionable boat operator/DMC"},{"name":"Corveta Ipiranga wreck (~62m)","si_tag":"diveglobal","tier":"premier","commission_path":"premium tech-dive package","source":"https://bahia.ws/en/naufragio-da-corveta-ipiranga-no-arquipelago-de-fernando-de-noronha/","si":"diveglobal","commission":"premium tech-dive package"},{"name":"Caverna de Sapata (~18m)","si_tag":"diveglobal","tier":"comfort","commission_path":"guided reef-dive package","source":"https://bahia.ws/en/mergulho-em-fernando-de-noronha/","si":"diveglobal","commission":"guided reef-dive package"},{"name":"Atalaia dive/snorkel zone (8-22m)","si_tag":"diveglobal","tier":"comfort","commission_path":"dive-operator day trip","source":"https://bahia.ws/en/mergulho-em-fernando-de-noronha/","si":"diveglobal","commission":"dive-operator day trip"},{"name":"Baia dos Golfinhos dawn watch","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"essential","commission_path":"guided dawn eco-tour (no-entry viewpoint)","source":"https://www.tripadvisor.com/Attraction_Review-g616328-d2391494-Reviews-Baia_do_Sancho-Fernando_de_Noronha_State_of_Pernambuco.html","si":"expedition","commission":"guided dawn eco-tour (no-entry viewpoint)"},{"name":"Atalaia natural pool (guided/capped)","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"comfort","commission_path":"ICMBio permit (pass-through) + guided eco add-on","source":"https://www.parnanoronha.com.br/en/atrativos","hook":"reported variously. Treat as strictly capped, guide-mandatory, book-on-arrival. Confirm the day''s rule with ICMBio","si":"expedition","blurb":"reported variously. Treat as strictly capped, guide-mandatory, book-on-arrival. Confirm the day''s rule with ICMBio","commission":"ICMBio permit (pass-through) + guided eco add-on"},{"name":"Projeto Tamar visitor center","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"essential","commission_path":"eco-tour visit inside guided day","source":"https://www.natalriograndedonorte.com/projeto-tamar-fernando-de-noronha/","si":"expedition","commission":"eco-tour visit inside guided day"}],"faq":[{"q":"When is the best time to dive Fernando de Noronha?","a":"August–November is the dive peak because the dry season delivers the clearest water and calmest seas, with the September–October visibility apex reaching up to ~50 m. April–June (rainy) is the diver''s value window — rain hits the surface, not the reef, so visibility stays strong and the island is quieter.","source":"planetaexo.com, Accessed 2026-07-07","si_tag":"liveaboard"},{"q":"How do you get to Baía do Sancho?","a":"Baía do Sancho is reached only by boat or by a staircase carved into the volcanic rock face, and a marine-park pass is required. It has been voted the best beach in the world by TripAdvisor travelers five times, which is why access is deliberately controlled.","source":"tripadvisor.com, Accessed 2026-07-07","si_tag":"tropical"},{"q":"Which is the best honeymoon pousada on Fernando de Noronha?","a":"Pousada Maravilha is consistently ranked the island''s top honeymoon hotel, with six sea-facing apartments plus bungalows with private hot tubs, an infinity pool, fine dining and a spa. Nannai Noronha (10 bungalows, private verandas, direct beach access) is the other ultra-tier couples pick.","source":"boutiquetravelexperts.com, Accessed 2026-07-07","si_tag":"romance"},{"q":"Can you swim with the spinner dolphins at Baía dos Golfinhos?","a":"No — Baía dos Golfinhos is a no-entry protected dolphin resting bay: no descending, no swimming, no boats inside. Spinner dolphins are watched from a clifftop viewpoint, best at first light. This is a legal protection, not a suggestion.","source":"tripadvisor.com, Accessed 2026-07-07","si_tag":"expedition"},{"q":"Is Fernando de Noronha safe right now?","a":"Yes — it is freely bookable at Level 2, with `book_enabled = true` and no consent flow. Brazil''s L2 is driven by mainland urban crime and kidnapping, with favelas rated Level 4; none of that reaches the archipelago, a controlled-access national marine park and one of Brazil''s lowest-risk environments.","source":"travel.state.gov, Accessed 2026-07-07","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"What''s the real risk to plan for?","a":"Remoteness and medical evacuation. Fernando de Noronha has a hyperbaric chamber adjacent to Hospital São Lucas, but the hospital provides basic emergency care only — serious trauma or complex decompression illness requires evacuation to the mainland (Recife/Natal), and weather can delay the flight. Carry insurance with medevac and dive conservatively.","source":"divejourney.io, Accessed 2026-07-07","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"Is diving the Corveta Ipiranga wreck dangerous?","a":"It is technical / Extended-Range diving: the wreck sits at ~62 m off Ponta da Sapata, so operators require Nitrox plus ~50 logged dives and evaluation dives before permitting it, always with a pro. Recreational divers stay on shallower 8–22 m reef and cave sites. Because you leave only by air, observe an 18–24 h surface interval before your flight.","source":"bahia.ws, Accessed 2026-07-07","si_tag":"safety"}],"seo":{"search_language":"pt-BR","jsonld_type":"TouristDestination","author_byline":"By David McCallister — commercial pilot, 56 countries","freshness":"2026-07-07","local_keywords":["Fernando de Noronha mergulho","Baia do Sancho","taxa ambiental Noronha","taxa de preservacao ambiental Noronha 2026","Pousada Maravilha lua de mel","piscina natural Atalaia"],"hreflang":["en","pt-BR"]},"booking":null,"si_checklist_25":null,"sis_present":null,"ultra":[{"name":"Pousada Maravilha","tier":"$$$$","lane":"Fora/Virtuoso","earning":"luxury commission + AOR; MoR on buyout","note":"island''s top honeymoon property"},{"name":"Nannai Noronha","tier":"$$$$","lane":"Fora/Virtuoso","earning":"luxury commission + dive attach; MoR villa-equivalent"},{"name":"Pousada Ze Maria","tier":"premier","lane":"premium romance","earning":"commissionable pousada + dining attach"},{"name":"Pousada Teju-Acu","tier":"premier","lane":"eco-luxury","earning":"commissionable boutique pousada + eco-tour attach"}],"source_verified":null,"hero":{"query":"Fernando de Noronha, Brazil, Brazil"},"geo":{"lat":-3.8547,"lng":-32.4248}}'::jsonb, 37),
  ('foz-do-iguacu-brazil', '10S', 'Foz do Iguaçu, Brazil', 'Brazil', 'Foz do Iguaçu', 'live', 'verified', 'mountainValley', 'Amazon, Pantanal & Iguaçu', '{"expedition","culture","romance"}', '{}', '{"essential","comfort","premier","luxury","ultra"}', null, null, '{"key_facts":null,"safety":{"emergency":"190","emergency_medical":"192","emergency_fire":"193","advisory_level":"L2","book_enabled":true,"bin":"freely bookable (L2)","consent_flow":false,"air_access_verified":true,"air_access_note":"Foz do Iguaçu / Cataratas International Airport (IGU / SBFI), 13 km / ~8 mi from downtown, minutes from the park entrance; LATAM/Azul/Gol","hazards":["wet slippery falls walkways","Macuco boat full-soak / life vests mandatory","helicopter aviation","Argentine-side border crossing","Ciudad del Este / Paraguay-side petty crime","dengue"]},"timing":{"peak":["Mar-Apr","Aug-Sep"],"peak_note":"Best flow + weather; Apr-May the single best window","summer_note":"Dec-Feb hot/rainiest/highest-water but most crowded","dry_note":"Jun-Aug cooler/calmer but lower flow","inflection":["~February (into Mar-Apr peak)","~July (into Aug-Sep peak)"],"fire_date":"curve-start minus 1-2 weeks — mid-to-late January (Mar-Apr travel) and late June (Aug-Sep travel)","off_season_fill":"Dec-Feb: sell max-roar high-water spectacle + Belmond honeymoon; bundle Itaipu-by-night + Parque das Aves"},"jewels":[{"si_tag":"expedition","name":"Trilha das Cataratas panoramic walkway + Devil''s Throat balcony","tier":"essential","commission_path":"park entry non-commissionable; guided-trail + transfer margin via DMC/OTA","source":"https://iguazufalls-tickets.org/what-to-see/iguazu-falls-brazil-side-viewpoints/ (Accessed 2026-07-07)","timing":"[''Mar-Apr'', ''Aug-Sep'']","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"The defining Brazilian-side experience: 1.4-km rim walk to the wide-angle Devil''s Throat view and panoramic elevator","si":"expedition","blurb":"The defining Brazilian-side experience: 1.4-km rim walk to the wide-angle Devil''s Throat view and panoramic elevator","when":"[''Mar-Apr'', ''Aug-Sep'']","commission":"park entry non-commissionable; guided-trail + transfer margin via DMC/OTA","accessed":"2026-07-07"},{"si_tag":"expedition","name":"Macuco Safari — boat under the falls","tier":"comfort","commission_path":"OTA affiliate on operator margin; park-entry portion non-commissionable; from ~US$109/adult","source":"https://www.viator.com/tours/Foz-do-Iguacu/Macuco-Safari-Boat-Ride/d970-7558P14 (Accessed 2026-07-07)","timing":"[''Mar-Apr'', ''Aug-Sep'']","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"The three-stage jungle-trail-boat run that soaks you beneath the cataracts","si":"expedition","blurb":"The three-stage jungle-trail-boat run that soaks you beneath the cataracts","when":"[''Mar-Apr'', ''Aug-Sep'']","commission":"OTA affiliate on operator margin; park-entry portion non-commissionable; from ~US$109/adult","accessed":"2026-07-07"},{"si_tag":"expedition","name":"Helicopter over the falls (Helisul)","tier":"premier","commission_path":"OTA affiliate; US$120-166/pp; 7-seat cap","source":"https://www.viator.com/tours/Foz-do-Iguacu/Panoramic-Helicopter-Flight-Iguazu-Falls-by-Helisul-Aviation/d970-216404P1 (Accessed 2026-07-07)","timing":"[''Mar-Apr'', ''Aug-Sep'']","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"10–12 min, both sides + Devil''s Throat in one frame, 7-seat cap","si":"expedition","blurb":"10–12 min, both sides + Devil''s Throat in one frame, 7-seat cap","when":"[''Mar-Apr'', ''Aug-Sep'']","commission":"OTA affiliate; US$120-166/pp; 7-seat cap","accessed":"2026-07-07"},{"si_tag":"expedition","name":"Sunrise-before-crowds at the falls (in-park hotel)","tier":"luxury","commission_path":"Belmond via Virtuoso/Fora consortium","source":"https://www.foratravel.com/trip-reports/A84HTP/a-stay-at-brazils-only-hotel-within-iguazu-falls-belmond-das-cataratas-saima-khan (Accessed 2026-07-07)","timing":"[''Mar-Apr'', ''Aug-Sep'']","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"Only Belmond das Cataratas guests walk the trails before the 9am public opening — the falls, alone, at first light","si":"expedition","blurb":"Only Belmond das Cataratas guests walk the trails before the 9am public opening — the falls, alone, at first light","when":"[''Mar-Apr'', ''Aug-Sep'']","commission":"Belmond via Virtuoso/Fora consortium","accessed":"2026-07-07"},{"si_tag":"romance","name":"Belmond das Cataratas terrace at sunset","tier":"luxury","commission_path":"hotel booking via preferred consortium","source":"https://www.belmond.com/hotels/south-america/brazil/iguassu-falls/belmond-hotel-das-cataratas/location (Accessed 2026-07-07)","timing":"[''Mar-Apr'', ''Aug-Sep'']","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"Caipirinha on the restaurant terrace as the sun sets behind the falls — the honeymoon set-piece","si":"romance","blurb":"Caipirinha on the restaurant terrace as the sun sets behind the falls — the honeymoon set-piece","when":"[''Mar-Apr'', ''Aug-Sep'']","commission":"hotel booking via preferred consortium","accessed":"2026-07-07"},{"si_tag":"romance","name":"Argentine-side full-day Devil''s Throat catwalk","tier":"comfort","commission_path":"guided cross-border transfer via DMC (border-crossing logistics = margin)","source":"https://www.rebeccaandtheworld.com/visiting-iguazu-falls-argentina-brazil-sides/ (Accessed 2026-07-07)","timing":"[''Mar-Apr'', ''Aug-Sep'']","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"The 1.1-km catwalk to the lip of Garganta del Diablo — the overwhelming close-range half of the wonder, framed as a romance day-adventure","si":"romance","blurb":"The 1.1-km catwalk to the lip of Garganta del Diablo — the overwhelming close-range half of the wonder, framed as a romance day-adventure","when":"[''Mar-Apr'', ''Aug-Sep'']","commission":"guided cross-border transfer via DMC (border-crossing logistics = margin)","accessed":"2026-07-07"},{"si_tag":"culture","name":"Parque das Aves","tier":"essential","commission_path":"OTA admission + guided-tour margin","source":"https://www.tripadvisor.com/Attraction_Review-g303444-d737277-Reviews-Parque_das_Aves-Foz_do_Iguacu_State_of_Parana.html (Accessed 2026-07-07)","timing":"[''Mar-Apr'', ''Aug-Sep'']","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"beside the national park, holds more than 1,320 birds across roughly 143 species in 16.5 hectares of Atlantic Rainforest","si":"culture","blurb":"beside the national park, holds more than 1,320 birds across roughly 143 species in 16.5 hectares of Atlantic Rainforest","when":"[''Mar-Apr'', ''Aug-Sep'']","commission":"OTA admission + guided-tour margin","accessed":"2026-07-07"},{"si_tag":"culture","name":"Itaipu Dam Illuminated night tour","tier":"essential","commission_path":"official Itaipu tourism channel + OTA","source":"https://turismoitaipu.com.br/en/blog/Itaipu-tour-illuminated-Foz-at-night/ (Accessed 2026-07-07)","timing":"[''Mar-Apr'', ''Aug-Sep'']","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"sold via the official Itaipu tourism channel and OTAs; a strong length-of-stay extender","si":"culture","blurb":"sold via the official Itaipu tourism channel and OTAs; a strong length-of-stay extender","when":"[''Mar-Apr'', ''Aug-Sep'']","commission":"official Itaipu tourism channel + OTA","accessed":"2026-07-07"},{"si_tag":"culture","name":"Triple-frontier viewpoint (Marco das Três Fronteiras)","tier":"essential","commission_path":"guided-tour margin; kept on the safe Brazilian bank away from Ciudad del Este","source":"https://greydynamics.com/gangsters-paradise-south-americas-triple-frontier/ (Accessed 2026-07-07)","timing":"year-round","timing_type":"ALWAYS-ON","si":"culture","when":"year-round","commission":"guided-tour margin; kept on the safe Brazilian bank away from Ciudad del Este","accessed":"2026-07-07"}],"faq":[{"q":"When is the best time to visit the Brazilian side of Iguaçu Falls?","a":"March–April and August–September are the sweet spots — comfortable 20–30°C, still-high water from the summer rains, and far smaller crowds than the December–February peak; April–May is widely called the single best window, with near-full flow, cooled temperatures and thinned crowds.","source":"iguazufalls-tickets.org, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"expedition"},{"q":"Why stay at the Belmond Hotel das Cataratas?","a":"Because it is the only hotel inside Brazil''s Iguaçu National Park, its guests get the falls essentially alone — walking the trails before the 9am public opening and after the 5pm closing, the dawn-and-dusk private-falls access that no city hotel can match.","source":"foratravel.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"romance"},{"q":"What''s worth doing besides the falls themselves?","a":"Two standouts extend the stay: the Itaipu Dam \"Illuminated\" night tour lights one of the world''s largest hydroelectric plants with 747 spotlights and 112 luminaires, and Parque das Aves next to the park immerses you among 1,320+ birds across roughly 143 species.","source":"turismoitaipu.com.br, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"culture"},{"q":"Is Foz do Iguaçu safe to visit right now?","a":"Yes, when you route to the park: Brazil sits at Level 2 and the 100-mile border strip carries an internal Level 4, but the State Department explicitly exempts the destination — *\"Travel to the Foz do Iguacu National Park and Pantanal National Park is allowed.\"* `book_enabled = true`, no consent flow.","source":"travel.state.gov, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"What''s the real risk to plan for around the falls?","a":"The tri-border corridor: the Brazil–Argentina–Paraguay triple frontier is a known smuggling and money-laundering zone, but the Iguazu tourist corridor stays accessible with normal precautions — it''s the Paraguay-side Ciudad del Este shopping run that carries elevated petty-crime and after-dark risk, so advise clients away from it unless escorted.","source":"greydynamics.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"Is the Macuco Safari boat trip dangerous?","a":"No, when run with the operator: it''s a guided-only, three-stage run of roughly 1 hr 45 min (about 30 min on the water) with mandatory life vests issued at the dock — expect to get completely soaked, so leave anything not waterproof behind.","source":"iguazufalls.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"safety"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"Foz do Iguaçu, Brazil — Iguaçu Falls Panoramic Side, In-Park Belmond & Macuco Safari | TravelWell.World","meta_description":"Plan the Brazilian side of Iguaçu Falls — the wide-angle Devil''s Throat, the boat under the cataracts, the only in-park hotel, and how to time your visit for peak flow.","search_language":"pt-BR","local_keywords":["Cataratas do Iguaçu","Macuco Safari","Parque das Aves","Trilha das Cataratas","Garganta do Diabo","Usina de Itaipu iluminada","melhor época para visitar as Cataratas"],"long_tail_en":["Iguaçu Falls Brazil side vs Argentina side","best time to visit Iguaçu Falls Brazilian side","only hotel inside Iguaçu National Park Brazil","Macuco Safari boat under the falls","helicopter tour over Iguaçu Falls","is Foz do Iguaçu safe to visit"],"hreflang":["en","pt-BR"],"jsonld_type":"TouristDestination","author_byline":"By David McCallister — commercial pilot, 56 countries","freshness":"2026-07-07","primary_keyword":"Foz do Iguaçu"},"booking":null,"si_checklist_25":null,"sis_present":[{"si":"expedition","status":"live"},{"si":"culture","status":"live"},{"si":"romance","status":"live"}],"ultra":[{"name":"Belmond Hotel das Cataratas","side":"Brazil (in-park)","earning":"consortium commission on room + F&B + spa + VIP amenity/upgrade value","mor":"hotel (agent AOR via Fora/Virtuoso)","tier":"ULTRA","hook":"only hotel inside the Brazilian NP; dawn/dusk private falls access before 9am and after 5pm"},{"name":"Loi Suites Iguazú","side":"Argentina (cross-ref, outside park on approach road)","earning":"consortium commission via Scott Dunn / andBeyond-class partners","mor":"hotel","tier":"ULTRA (cross-ref, not primary)","hook":"5-star jungle lodge, 162 units on wooden bridges through Iryapú forest; note Sheraton Iguazú is the in-park Argentine option"}],"source_verified":null,"hero":{"query":"Foz do Iguaçu, Brazil, Brazil"},"geo":{"lat":-25.5163,"lng":-54.5854}}'::jsonb, 38),
  ('galapagos-islands-ecuador', '10S', 'The Galápagos Islands', 'Ecuador', 'Liveaboard weeks and island crossings **TravelWell', 'live', 'verified', 'oceanAerial', 'Andes (Quito) & Galápagos', '{"liveaboard","expedition"}', '{}', '{"comfort","premier","luxury","ultra"}', null, null, '{"key_facts":["Darwin and Wolf islands are reachable ONLY by liveaboard; most trips run 7 nights with up to 4 dives/day.","Galapagos is one of the only places on earth to reliably dive with whale sharks (10-12m adults), June-November, peak August-September.","During the June-November cool season ~90% of monitored hammerheads stay in the reserve; schools aggregate along the thermocline ~20-30m.","Galapagos National Park entry fee doubled to US$200 per foreign adult on 2024-08-01; INGALA/CGREG transit card (TCT) is a separate ~US$20-30.","Access is via Baltra/Seymour (GPS) or San Cristobal (SCY) on Avianca/LATAM flights from Quito (UIO) or Guayaquil (GYE) only."],"safety":{"emergency":"911","marine_vhf":"Channel 16","hyperbaric_chamber":"Puerto Ayora, Santa Cruz — Protesub S.A. / SSS Recompression Chamber Network (DAN referral center), 24/7, +593 5 252-6911. Only chamber in the islands; many hours by boat from Darwin/Wolf; serious cases medevac to mainland or US.","advisory_level":"L2","advisory_date":"2025-10-14","advisory_codes":"C (Crime) / T (Terrorism) / U (Unrest) / K (Kidnapping) — mainland-driven; islands not a named area","book_enabled":true,"bin":"freely bookable (L2)","consent_flow":"none (BIN 4 — standard L2 disclosure only)","l2_disclosure":true,"state_dept_carveout":"Galápagos and Quito explicitly NOT designated restricted; L4 zones are mainland-only (Esmeraldas city+north, Guayaquil south of Portete de Tarqui Ave., Duran, Huaquillas/Arenillas, Quevedo/Quinsaloma/Pueblo Viejo)","air_access_verified":true,"air_access":"GPS (Baltra/Seymour) and SCY (San Cristobal) via UIO (Quito) or GYE (Guayaquil) on Avianca/LATAM","no_fly_after_diving":"12h single no-deco / 18h multi-day repetitive / 24h recommended buffer before the island-to-mainland flight (note Quito altitude ~2,850m)","medevac_note":"State Dept warns serious illness/injury typically requires medical evacuation; recommends evacuation insurance $60,000+","other":"open-Pacific seasickness (long overnight Darwin/Wolf crossings roughest); extreme equatorial sun; DAN dive insurance with evac coverage effectively mandatory"},"timing":{"type":"dive-calendar-two-season","dive_calendar":true,"warm_snorkel_season":"December-May (warmer water ~25-27C, calm seas, best snorkel/land wildlife; family + honeymoon)","big_marine_dive_season":"June-November (cool ~16-24C, strong currents; hammerhead schools + whale sharks at Darwin & Wolf)","peak":"July-August + whale-shark peak August-September + mid-December-early-January holidays","dive_curve_start":"2026-06-01","warm_curve_start":"2026-12-01","booking_lead_months":"6-12 (top liveaboard cabins + premium expedition suites; whale-shark weeks and holidays sell first)","shoulder_off_season_fill":"April-May and September-October","fire_date":"2026-05-18","trigger_date":"2026-05-18","secondary_fire_date":"2026-11-15","sharpen_note":"sharpen on live tracking — Aggressor / expedition-cruise availability feeds + hammerhead & whale-shark sighting logs; upwelling onset and pelagic aggregation shift yearly"},"jewels":[{"name":"Darwin''s Arch / Darwin Island","si_tag":"Dive Liveaboards/GEA","tier":"premier","commission_path":"own-CLIA / TCI Land Agency lane (Galápagos Aggressor III) — the moat","source":"https://www.naturetripper.com/articles/whale-sharks-galapagos","timing":"July-August + whale-shark peak August-September + mid-December-early-January holidays","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"Dive Liveaboards/GEA","when":"July-August + whale-shark peak August-September + mid-December-early-January holidays","commission":"own-CLIA / TCI Land Agency lane (Galápagos Aggressor III) — the moat"},{"name":"Wolf Island","si_tag":"Dive Liveaboards/GEA","tier":"premier","commission_path":"own-CLIA liveaboard lane — the moat","source":"https://www.dive-the-world.com/posts/darwin-wolf/galapagos-islands-diving-trips-darwin-and-wolf-islands.php","timing":"July-August + whale-shark peak August-September + mid-December-early-January holidays","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"Dive Liveaboards/GEA","when":"July-August + whale-shark peak August-September + mid-December-early-January holidays","commission":"own-CLIA liveaboard lane — the moat"},{"name":"Gordon Rocks (off Santa Cruz)","si_tag":"Dive Liveaboards/GEA","tier":"comfort","commission_path":"own-CLIA liveaboard lane or AFF day-boat from Puerto Ayora","source":"https://www.aggressor.com/kbyg_document/galapagos","timing":"July-August + whale-shark peak August-September + mid-December-early-January holidays","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"Dive Liveaboards/GEA","when":"July-August + whale-shark peak August-September + mid-December-early-January holidays","commission":"own-CLIA liveaboard lane or AFF day-boat from Puerto Ayora"},{"name":"Kicker Rock / León Dormido (off San Cristóbal)","si_tag":"Dive Liveaboards/GEA","tier":"comfort","commission_path":"own-CLIA liveaboard lane or AFF day-operator from San Cristóbal","source":"https://www.oars.com/adventures/galapagos-origins-of-species/","timing":"July-August + whale-shark peak August-September + mid-December-early-January holidays","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"Dive Liveaboards/GEA","when":"July-August + whale-shark peak August-September + mid-December-early-January holidays","commission":"own-CLIA liveaboard lane or AFF day-operator from San Cristóbal"},{"name":"Cabo Marshall / Cabo Douglas & Punta Vicente Roca (Isabela/Fernandina)","si_tag":"liveaboard","tier":"premier","commission_path":"own-CLIA liveaboard lane","source":"https://www.aggressor.com/kbyg_document/galapagos","timing":"July-August + whale-shark peak August-September + mid-December-early-January holidays","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"liveaboard","when":"July-August + whale-shark peak August-September + mid-December-early-January holidays","commission":"own-CLIA liveaboard lane"},{"name":"Bartolomé — Pinnacle Rock","si_tag":"GEA/Romance","tier":"luxury","commission_path":"Fora/Virtuoso expedition-cruise lane","source":"https://ecolodgesanywhere.com/galapagos-islands/","timing":"July-August + whale-shark peak August-September + mid-December-early-January holidays","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"GEA/Romance","when":"July-August + whale-shark peak August-September + mid-December-early-January holidays","commission":"Fora/Virtuoso expedition-cruise lane"},{"name":"Española — Punta Suárez (waved albatross)","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"luxury","commission_path":"Fora/Virtuoso expedition-cruise lane","source":"https://ecolodgesanywhere.com/galapagos-islands/","timing":"year-round","timing_type":"ALWAYS-ON","si":"expedition","when":"year-round","commission":"Fora/Virtuoso expedition-cruise lane"},{"name":"Genovesa — Bird Island","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"luxury","commission_path":"Fora/Virtuoso expedition-cruise lane","source":"https://ecolodgesanywhere.com/galapagos-islands/","timing":"July-August + whale-shark peak August-September + mid-December-early-January holidays","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"expedition","when":"July-August + whale-shark peak August-September + mid-December-early-January holidays","commission":"Fora/Virtuoso expedition-cruise lane"},{"name":"Charles Darwin Research Station + giant tortoises (Santa Cruz)","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"comfort","commission_path":"AFF/day lane add-on to a Fora hotel/cruise booking","source":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Puerto_Ayora","timing":"July-August + whale-shark peak August-September + mid-December-early-January holidays","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"expedition","when":"July-August + whale-shark peak August-September + mid-December-early-January holidays","commission":"AFF/day lane add-on to a Fora hotel/cruise booking"},{"name":"Isabela — Sierra Negra volcano & Galápagos penguins","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"comfort","commission_path":"AFF day-operator lane; Fora if bundled in a land package","source":"https://www.kimkim.com/c/galapagos-snorkeling-wildlife-tour-7-days","si":"expedition","commission":"AFF day-operator lane; Fora if bundled in a land package"},{"name":"Los Túneles (Cabo Rosa, Isabela)","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"comfort","commission_path":"AFF day-operator lane","source":"https://www.kimkim.com/c/galapagos-snorkeling-wildlife-tour-7-days","timing":"July-August + whale-shark peak August-September + mid-December-early-January holidays","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"expedition","when":"July-August + whale-shark peak August-September + mid-December-early-January holidays","commission":"AFF day-operator lane"},{"name":"Tortuga Bay (Santa Cruz)","si_tag":"GEA/Romance","tier":"comfort","commission_path":"AFF/day lane (self-guided) add-on to a Fora hotel booking","source":"https://www.kimkim.com/c/galapagos-snorkeling-wildlife-tour-7-days","timing":"July-August + whale-shark peak August-September + mid-December-early-January holidays","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"GEA/Romance","when":"July-August + whale-shark peak August-September + mid-December-early-January holidays","commission":"AFF/day lane (self-guided) add-on to a Fora hotel booking"}],"faq":[{"q":"Is the Galápagos safe given Ecuador''s travel advisory?","a":"Yes — freely bookable. Ecuador is US State Dept Level 2, but the Galápagos and Quito are explicitly NOT restricted; the Level 4 \"Do Not Travel\" zones (Esmeraldas, parts of Guayaquil, Durán) are mainland-only, and the islands sit ~1,000 km offshore, insulated from mainland gang conflict. Guests transit UIO or GYE airport straight to the island flight.","source":"travel.state.gov, reissued 2025-10-14","si_tag":""},{"q":"How dangerous is diving Darwin and Wolf — can beginners do it?","a":"No — these are advanced dives, not a beginner destination. Reputable operators gate Darwin/Wolf on Advanced Open Water certification plus logged current/cold-water experience: divers hook onto ledges in ripping current at 20–30 m in 16–24 °C water, far from support. Gordon Rocks and Kicker Rock are the intermediate-to-advanced warm-ups.","source":"aggressor.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"liveaboard"},{"q":"How long should I wait to fly after diving the Galápagos?","a":"Plan a full 18–24 hours before the island-to-mainland flight. A liveaboard week is repetitive multi-day diving (DAN: 18 h minimum, 24 h recommended), and Quito sits at ~2,850 m — so never book a same-day-as-last-dive flight. The only hyperbaric chamber is in Puerto Ayora, hours by boat from Darwin/Wolf, so DAN evacuation insurance is effectively mandatory.","source":"DAN guidance via sssnetwork.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"dive-safety"},{"q":"When is the best time to dive for hammerheads and whale sharks?","a":"June–November — the cool, plankton-rich season — is the big-animal window, with whale sharks peaking August–September, because the Humboldt upwelling drops water to 16–24 °C and concentrates pelagic life; ~90% of monitored hammerheads stay in the reserve then, schooling in the hundreds. Expect cooler water and stronger current.","source":"galapagossharkdiving.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"liveaboard"},{"q":"Do I need a cruise, or can I stay on land?","a":"Both work, but the iconic sites need a boat. Darwin and Wolf are liveaboard-only, and by park rule every visitor-site landing must be led by a licensed naturalist guide. Land-based island-hopping (Santa Cruz, Isabela) covers tortoises, Tortuga Bay and day dives; the deep wildlife (Española albatross, Genovesa seabirds) needs an expedition cruise.","source":"oars.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"expedition"},{"q":"What''s the best Galápagos trip for a honeymoon?","a":"A small all-suite expedition yacht or the highlands Pikaia Lodge. The warm season (Dec–May, water 25–27 °C, calm seas) is the easiest for first-timers and snorkeling; book 6–12 months ahead because the top cabins and suites — and holiday sailings — sell out first.","source":"galapagossharkdiving.com / dive-the-world.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"romance"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"Galápagos Diving & Expedition Cruises — Darwin & Wolf Liveaboards, Hammerheads, Whale Sharks | TravelWell.World","jsonld_type":"TouristDestination","author_byline":"By David McCallister — commercial pilot, 56 countries","content_freshness":"2026-07-07","search_language":"es-EC","local_keywords":["Galapagos liveaboard diving","Darwin Wolf hammerheads","Galapagos cruise","Galapagos whale shark diving","Galapagos Aggressor III","best time to dive Galapagos","Galapagos expedition cruise","islas Galápagos crucero","bucear Galápagos","crucero de buceo Galápagos","tiburón ballena Galápagos","no fly after diving Galapagos"],"hreflang":["en","es-EC"]},"booking":null,"si_checklist_25":null,"sis_present":["liveaboard","expedition"],"ultra":[{"name":"Aqua Mare (Aqua Expeditions) — 16-guest superyacht","tier":"ultra","mor":"Fora / Virtuoso luxury-cruise lane; full-yacht buyout = villa-equivalent","source":"https://www.luxurytraveladvisor.com/cruises/wild-things"},{"name":"Silversea Silver Origin — 100-guest ultra-luxury expedition","tier":"luxury-ultra","mor":"Fora / Virtuoso luxury-cruise lane (Virtuoso-preferred)","source":"https://www.luxurytraveladvisor.com/cruises/wild-things"},{"name":"Celebrity Flora — 100-guest all-suite expedition","tier":"luxury-ultra","mor":"Fora / Virtuoso luxury-cruise lane","source":"https://www.luxurytraveladvisor.com/cruises/wild-things"},{"name":"Ecoventura Origin / Theory / Evolve — 20-guest all-suite (Relais & Châteaux)","tier":"luxury-ultra","mor":"Fora / Virtuoso luxury-cruise lane (Relais & Châteaux)","source":"https://www.luxurytraveladvisor.com/cruises/wild-things"},{"name":"Pikaia Lodge (Santa Cruz highlands, Relais & Châteaux + private yacht)","tier":"luxury-ultra","mor":"Fora lane (host-agency IATA)","source":"https://www.mrandmrssmith.com/luxury-hotels/pikaia-lodge"},{"name":"Private full-yacht charter (Aggressor III buyout / all-suite expedition buyout)","tier":"ultra","mor":"own-CLIA / TCI Land Agency lane — convertible affiliate->commissioned-agent (the moat)","source":"https://www.aggressor.com/destination/galapagos"}],"source_verified":"2026-07-07","hero":{"query":"The Galápagos Islands, Ecuador"},"geo":{"lat":-0.9538,"lng":-90.9656}}'::jsonb, 39),
  ('granada-nicaragua', '10S', 'Granada, Nicaragua', 'Nicaragua', 'Granada', 'live', 'verified', 'kyoto', 'Nicaragua', '{"culture"}', '{}', '{"essential","comfort"}', null, null, '{"key_facts":null,"safety":{"emergency":"118","emergency_all":{"police":"118","ambulance_red_cross":"128","fire":"115 / 911 (cell)","tourist_line":"101"},"advisory_date":"2026-05-14","advisory_codes":["C","H","D","O"],"book_enabled":false,"bin":"NO SAFE ZONE (content-only)","content_only":true,"redirect_eligible":true,"consent_flow":null,"trauma":"limited outside Managua; comprehensive care Managua-only → US medevac","founder_review_flag":"WHY = country-wide political detention (targets perceived govt opponents/NGO/journalist/dual-national/property); may not reach a typical short-stay Granada tourist — reconsideration is a founder/attorney call, NOT a CC call. Flagged, not decided.","source":"https://travel.state.gov/content/travel/en/traveladvisories/traveladvisories/nicaragua-travel-advisory.html + Accessed 2026-07-07"},"timing":{"peak":"Nov–Apr (dry season)","inflection":"May & Oct shoulder; Jun–Sep wet/low","off_season":"Jun–Sep wetter, quieter","fire_date":"held — pending advisory clearance + founder/attorney"},"jewels":[{"name":"Catedral de Granada","si_tag":"culture","tier":"essential","commission_path":"non-commissionable","source":"https://onaroadtonowhere.com/2025/02/25/granada-nicaragua-a-colonial-beauty-that-might-steal-your-heart/ + Accessed 2026-07-07","timing":"Nov–Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"the yellow-and-white bell towers and crimson domes over Parque Central","si":"culture","blurb":"the yellow-and-white bell towers and crimson domes over Parque Central","when":"Nov–Apr","commission":"non-commissionable","accessed":"2026-07-07"},{"name":"Calle La Calzada","si_tag":"culture","tier":"essential","commission_path":"non-commissionable","source":"https://www.tripadvisor.com/Attraction_Review-g580113-d2707513-Reviews-Calle_La_Calzada-Granada_Granada_Department.html + Accessed 2026-07-07","timing":"Nov–Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"the lively colonial spine of the city; colorful façades, restaurants and bars, live music and salsa after sunset","si":"culture","blurb":"the lively colonial spine of the city; colorful façades, restaurants and bars, live music and salsa after sunset","when":"Nov–Apr","commission":"non-commissionable","accessed":"2026-07-07"},{"name":"Las Isletas (kayak/boat)","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"comfort","commission_path":"dormant","source":"https://www.viator.com/Nicaragua-attractions/Islets-of-Granada-Las-Isletas-de-Granada/d4499-a6931 + Accessed 2026-07-07","hook":"lifejackets, weather-aware; a captained boat is the norm. Content","si":"expedition","blurb":"lifejackets, weather-aware; a captained boat is the norm. Content","commission":"dormant","accessed":"2026-07-07"},{"name":"Mombacho cloud-forest + canopy","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"comfort","commission_path":"dormant","source":"https://www.viator.com/tours/Granada/Mombacho-Volcano-Cloud-Forest/d4853-69457P3 + Accessed 2026-07-07","timing":"Nov–Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"always with a park-authorized guide on the 4x4 + Crater Trail; cloud-forest footing is wet and steep. Content","si":"expedition","blurb":"always with a park-authorized guide on the 4x4 + Crater Trail; cloud-forest footing is wet and steep. Content","when":"Nov–Apr","commission":"dormant","accessed":"2026-07-07"},{"name":"Masaya active lava-lake (night) + Masaya market","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"comfort","commission_path":"dormant","source":"https://www.tripadvisor.com/AttractionProductReview-g580113-d12935426-Masaya_Volcano_Night_Tour_and_Apoyo_Lagoon-Granada_Granada_Department.html + Accessed 2026-07-07","hook":"molten glow from the crater rim; pair with Masaya artisan market by day for hammocks, ceramics, leather","si":"expedition","blurb":"molten glow from the crater rim; pair with Masaya artisan market by day for hammocks, ceramics, leather","commission":"dormant","accessed":"2026-07-07"},{"name":"Laguna de Apoyo swim","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"essential","commission_path":"dormant","source":"https://hiddennicaragua.com/2022/07/10/apoyo-lagoon-nicaragua/ + Accessed 2026-07-07","hook":"protected caldera lake, no motorboats, clean water; deep and steep-sided — swim near shore/lakeside spots. Content","si":"expedition","blurb":"protected caldera lake, no motorboats, clean water; deep and steep-sided — swim near shore/lakeside spots. Content","commission":"dormant","accessed":"2026-07-07"},{"name":"León day trip","si_tag":"culture","tier":"essential","commission_path":"dormant","source":"https://bbqboy.net/visiting-granada-volcan-masaya-and-laguna-de-apoyo-nicaragua/ + Accessed 2026-07-07","timing":"Nov–Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"Granada''s colonial rival/sibling city, an easy day out for churches and revolutionary-mural history","si":"culture","blurb":"Granada''s colonial rival/sibling city, an easy day out for churches and revolutionary-mural history","when":"Nov–Apr","commission":"dormant","accessed":"2026-07-07"}],"faq":[{"q":"Why is Granada worth visiting?","a":"Granada is the oldest city in Nicaragua and the oldest colonial city on the American mainland, settled in 1524 by conquistador Francisco Hernández de Córdoba. It claims to be the first European-established city on the mainland of the Americas, and its well-preserved colonial grid of pastel façades is the whole point of coming.","source":"costarica.org, Accessed 2026-07-07","si_tag":"culture"},{"q":"What are the best outdoor things to do around Granada?","a":"The signature outings are volcanoes and water. Las Isletas — 365 islets flung into Lake Nicaragua by a Mombacho eruption — are toured by boat or kayak; Mombacho''s cloud-forest is reached by 4x4 to a Crater Trail hike plus a canopy zip course; and Masaya''s night tour puts you at a crater-rim platform above an active lava lake.","source":"viator.com; tripadvisor.com, Accessed 2026-07-07","si_tag":"expedition"},{"q":"Where''s the best place to swim near Granada?","a":"Laguna de Apoyo, a crater lake about 25 minutes from Granada, is said to be the cleanest place to swim in all of Nicaragua because no motorboats are allowed on it. Day passes to lakeside spots run around $10 and include kayaks and loungers.","source":"hiddennicaragua.com, Accessed 2026-07-07","si_tag":"expedition"},{"q":"Is Granada a good honeymoon destination?","a":"Yes, on paper it is a natural romance set — private-island lodges, rooftop sunsets over Cocibolca, pastel streets. The ultra anchor is Jicaro Island Lodge, a National Geographic Unique Lodge with 9 two-story \"treehouse\" casitas on a private Las Isletas islet, with lakeside yoga and three multi-course meals included.","source":"jicaroisland.com, Accessed 2026-07-07","si_tag":"romance"},{"q":"Is Granada, Nicaragua safe to visit right now?","a":"Not on a bookable basis. Nicaragua carries a US State Department Level 3 — Reconsider Travel advisory, reissued May 14, 2026, with risk codes C/H/D/O. The driver is country-wide and political, with no named-safe geographic carve-out, so TravelWell keeps the Book path OFF; this page is content-only for the day it clears.","source":"travel.state.gov, Accessed 2026-07-07","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"What''s the real risk to plan for?","a":"Wrongful detention is the headline gatekeeper. Per the State Department, US nationals — including dual Nicaraguan-US citizens — are at serious risk of wrongful detention and may be held for years without due process, and authorities may seize property or search phones for anti-government content. A secondary risk is healthcare: comprehensive care exists only in Managua.","source":"travel.state.gov, Accessed 2026-07-07","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"Are the volcano hikes and lake trips dangerous?","a":"The activities themselves are guided and manageable, but they are content-only under the Level 3 advisory. Mombacho and Masaya are done with a park-authorized or licensed guide (volcanic-gas exposure and timed entry make it mandatory at Masaya), and Las Isletas boating requires lifejackets because Cocibolca can chop up fast.","source":"travel.state.gov, Accessed 2026-07-07","si_tag":"safety"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"Granada, Nicaragua Travel Guide — Colonial Jewel, Las Isletas & Volcanoes | TravelWell.World","jsonld_type":"TouristDestination","author_byline":"By David McCallister — commercial pilot, 56 countries","freshness":"2026-07-07","search_language":"es-NI","local_keywords":["qué hacer en Granada Nicaragua","Las Isletas","Volcán Masaya","Volcán Mombacho bosque nuboso","Laguna de Apoyo nadar","Catedral de Granada","Calle La Calzada"],"hreflang":["en","es-NI"],"primary_keyword":"Granada"},"booking":null,"si_checklist_25":null,"sis_present":[{"si":"culture","status":"live"}],"ultra":[{"name":"Jicaro Island Lodge","note":"NatGeo Unique Lodge, 9 treehouse casitas on private Las Isletas islet, spa/yoga, near-carbon-neutral","price_tier":"$$$$","commission_path":"dormant","source":"https://jicaroisland.com/ + Accessed 2026-07-07"},{"name":"Tribal Hotel","note":"boutique retreat in colonial core, garden + pool","price_tier":"$$$","commission_path":"dormant","source":"https://www.lightfoottravel.com/us/property/tribal-hotel + Accessed 2026-07-07"},{"name":"La Gran Francia / Hotel Plaza Colón","note":"restored colonial-mansion luxury on/near Parque Central","price_tier":"$$$","commission_path":"dormant","source":"https://voicesoftravel.com/where-to-stay-in-granada-nicaragua/ + Accessed 2026-07-07"}],"source_verified":null,"hero":{"query":"Granada, Nicaragua, Nicaragua"},"geo":{"lat":11.9344,"lng":-85.956}}'::jsonb, 40),
